window.COURSE={"title":"It's Not Macro-cket Science","by":"Benjamin Throssell","tagline":"How to eat what you want and get jacked doing it — all by using your macros.","modules":["HOW TO GET THE WHOLE HOG","HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","HOW TO EAT CAKE","HOW TO PUT INMRS TO WORK"],"lessons":[{"id":"how-i-lost-over-a-third-of-my-bodyweight-and-kept-it-off","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1999307387-fadf4b89bb871cd5c2cc2e710b02ea17241013e3f50cd06ad48ca28a9c250156-d_1280x720?region=us","n":1,"title":"How I lost OVER A THIRD of my bodyweight — and kept it off.","m":0,"vimeo":"1070723689","dur":335,"code":"0101","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET THE WHOLE HOG","How I lost OVER A THIRD of my bodyweight — and kept it off."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Let's skip the pleasantries. <p><br></p><p>You're here to get jacked. I'm here to make it happen.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Let's get to work 😎</strong></p>","text":"Let's skip the pleasantries. \nYou're here to get jacked. I'm here to make it happen.\nLet's get to work 😎"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1070723689","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1070723689?badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Do this now.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Do this now.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"Here's your checklist.<br><br><p><strong>A set of digital kitchen scales.</strong> I use a <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/littlescales\">microscale</a> for all my daily stuff, but I keep a <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/bigscales\">high capacity scale</a> on hand for when I do batch cooking. I find both handy, but I'd go with the microscales if you'd prefer only have one.<br><br></p><p><strong>A set of digital bathroom scales. </strong>They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea. <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/bathroomscales\">These</a> are the ones I use.<br><br></p><p><strong>A macro tracking app.</strong> I recommend <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/macrofactor\">MacroFactor</a> highly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A tape measure. </strong>This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a tape measure is a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line. I use <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/tape\">this</a> electronic one.<br></p><p><br></p><p>If you have analogue scales, I suggest making the switch to digital. If you’ve already got digital and they still work, then you can keep working with them. </p><p> </p><p>But let me say it one more time — <em>SKIP THIS IF YOU THINK IT'LL STOP YOU PROCEEDING.</em><br><em><br></em></p>","text":"Here's your checklist.\n\nA set of digital kitchen scales. I use a microscale for all my daily stuff, but I keep a high capacity scale on hand for when I do batch cooking. I find both handy, but I'd go with the microscales if you'd prefer only have one.\n\nA set of digital bathroom scales. They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea. These are the ones I use.\n\nA macro tracking app. I recommend MacroFactor highly.\nA tape measure. This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a tape measure is a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line. I use this electronic one.\n\nIf you have analogue scales, I suggest making the switch to digital. If you’ve already got digital and they still work, then you can keep working with them.  But let me say it one more time — SKIP THIS IF YOU THINK IT'LL STOP YOU PROCEEDING.","fixed_link":1}]}]},{"id":"the-most-valuable-video-of-inmrs-1","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1999309184-f702a2cab4152de1bc4aa329b4801b3fadb9470f9539df984d207e045af61d70-d_1280x720?region=us","n":2,"title":"The most valuable video of INMRS.","m":0,"vimeo":"1070724438","dur":298,"code":"0102","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET THE WHOLE HOG","The most valuable video of INMRS."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"If you watch <em>just this video...</em>","text":"If you watch just this video..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"You will be leagues ahead of anyone else starting a diet.","html":"<p>You will be <u>leagues ahead of anyone else</u> starting a diet. </p>"},{"type":"text","html":"And the way you approach your nutrition? <p><br></p><p>It'll never be the same 😌<em></em></p>","text":"And the way you approach your nutrition? \nIt'll never be the same 😌"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1070724438","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1070724438?badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"⚠️ Before you go any further...","html":"<p>⚠️ Before you go any further...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><em>THIS COURSE SHOULD BE TAKEN ON A DESKTOP.</em></strong><br></p>","text":"THIS COURSE SHOULD BE TAKEN ON A DESKTOP.","desk":1},{"type":"text","html":"<p> This hosting platform struggles to reformat to mobile. I strongly recommend you use a desktop to make sure that you have the best experience possible, and don't miss out on anything being delivered as it was designed. Some sections hold up okay, but sections with tables and so on just don't hold up well.<br></p><p><br></p><p>Benjamin.</p>","text":"This hosting platform struggles to reformat to mobile. I strongly recommend you use a desktop to make sure that you have the best experience possible, and don't miss out on anything being delivered as it was designed. Some sections hold up okay, but sections with tables and so on just don't hold up well.\n\nBenjamin."}],"desk":1}]},{"id":"this-entire-course-on-a-page","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1999309263-f0e707fe18c5ed1c83e24ef04da7e3327f6cf474613d783c5d8cac32985a162e-d_1280x720?region=us","n":3,"title":"This entire course on a page.","m":0,"vimeo":"1070725185","dur":208,"code":"0103","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET THE WHOLE HOG","This entire course on a page."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"This video is exactly what it says it is.","text":"This video is exactly what it says it is."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"I'm about to give you this entire course on a single page 😛","html":"<p>I'm about to give you <u>this entire course</u> on a single page 😛</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Get stuck in, and get a snapshot of the big picture, right now.","text":"Get stuck in, and get a snapshot of the big picture, right now."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1070725185","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1070725185?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"how-to-get-an-absolutely-unreasonable-roi","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1999309510-c53a2fad7001b1c643214b971083e9b1d064d12cf76694c07013b57d616f13d4-d_1280x720?region=us","n":4,"title":"How to get an absolutely unreasonable ROI.","m":0,"vimeo":"1070725609","dur":188,"code":"0104","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET THE WHOLE HOG","How to get an absolutely unreasonable ROI."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"This is the skinny on getting <strong>big, <em>fat returns</em></strong> on your investment.","text":"This is the skinny on getting big, fat returns on your investment."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1070725609","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1070725609?badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>There's gonna be friction to start,</strong> and it'll be hard to get your flywheel turning. But I'm telling ya — <em>it's worth the work. </em>And...<br></p>","text":"There's gonna be friction to start, and it'll be hard to get your flywheel turning. But I'm telling ya — it's worth the work. And..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The faster you get on the right side of the Rule of Ten... the crazier the gains get 🤯","html":"<p>The faster you get on the right side of the Rule of Ten... the <em>crazier </em>the gains get 🤯</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p> So, <u>sprint through this course<em></em></u> and get yourself there ASAP.<br></p><p><br></p><p>In the very next video, I'll show you how to completely skip what every rookie screws up when they start.</p>","text":"So, sprint through this course and get yourself there ASAP.\n\nIn the very next video, I'll show you how to completely skip what every rookie screws up when they start."}]},{"id":"ground-zero","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985115651-7293909ce6ff4987e741e140b1375521252d1e1e0c3922c1aa4f52404f39e97d-d_1280x720?region=us","n":5,"title":"Ground Zero.","m":1,"vimeo":"1058515000","dur":37,"code":"0201","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","Ground Zero."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>If I was a chump coach, I'd have skipped making this section for you 😒<br></p><p></p>","text":"If I was a chump coach, I'd have skipped making this section for you 😒"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>But winners do the work — and the </strong><em><strong>doggies get </strong></em><em><strong>jacked — </strong></em><strong>because we laid the right foundations.</strong></p><p></p>","text":"But winners do the work — and the doggies get jacked — because we laid the right foundations."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>In this section, you're about to skip the rookie mistakes that could add <em>months </em>to your journey. We're going to cover...</p><p><br></p><p></p><ul><li><strong>Why macro calculators SUCK</strong>, and what you can do to <em>instantly </em>juice up their accuracy...<br><br></li><li><strong>The easiest way</strong> to <u>guarantee</u> your targets are flat out <em>wrong </em>for you...<br><br></li><li><strong>An easy-to-find stat that'll skyrocket your chances</strong> of getting jacked without the speedbumps...</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Let's get stuck in.</p><p></p>","text":"In this section, you're about to skip the rookie mistakes that could add months to your journey. We're going to cover...\nWhy macro calculators SUCK, and what you can do to instantly juice up their accuracy...\n\nThe easiest way to guarantee your targets are flat out wrong for you...\n\nAn easy-to-find stat that'll skyrocket your chances of getting jacked without the speedbumps...\nLet's get stuck in."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058515000","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058515000?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"why-you-cant-trust-macro-calculators","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985115961-9d7e1737ebdca0c7752b7c2148dec924abadef64a47730476ef615528eca63c2-d_1280x720?region=us","n":6,"title":"Why you can't trust macro calculators.","m":1,"vimeo":"1058515465","dur":251,"code":"0202","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","Why you can't trust macro calculators."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Oh, so you want<em> perfect macro targets</em> out of your calculator? I got bad news...<br></p>","text":"Oh, so you want perfect macro targets out of your calculator? I got bad news..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Not a chance 🙃","html":"<p><em>Not a chance </em>🙃<br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Or, a slim one at best. </p><p><br></p><p>But in this video, I'll tell you <em>exactly </em>what's wrong with trusting a calculator for this, and what you can do about it.</p>","text":"Or, a slim one at best. \nBut in this video, I'll tell you exactly what's wrong with trusting a calculator for this, and what you can do about it."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058515465","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058515465?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"wanna-instantly-screw-your-macros-do-this","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985117291-6c165e0ad482c410dff5fd12de19b6170a87e81cc32aecbb1142e56ec29840cb-d_1280x720?region=us","n":7,"title":"Wanna instantly screw your macros? Do this...","m":1,"vimeo":"1058520454","dur":263,"code":"0203","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","Wanna instantly screw your macros? Do this..."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"There are two things absolutely <em><strong>essential</strong> </em>to your success, and...","text":"There are two things absolutely essential to your success, and..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"There's one way you can absolutely guarantee you screw them up 😵‍💫","html":"<p>There's one way you can absolutely guarantee you screw them up 😵‍💫</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>In this video, I break down the macro math mistake you gotta avoid <em>at all costs.</em></p>","text":"In this video, I break down the macro math mistake you gotta avoid at all costs."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058520454","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058520454?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Calculating your bodyfat.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Calculating your bodyfat.<br></p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"Here's how to tackle calculating your bodyfat.","text":"Here's how to tackle calculating your bodyfat."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Option One — DEXA scan","html":"<p><em>Option One — DEXA scan</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p> DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a flashy type of X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months. <br></p><p><br></p><p>To get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with...<br></p>","text":"DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a flashy type of X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months. \n\nTo get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Option Two — The Naval Method","html":"<p><em>Option Two — The Naval Method</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and a calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.</p><p><br></p><p>All your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:<br><br></p><p><strong></strong></p><p><strong>Neck - </strong>Measure at the base of your neck.<br></p><p><strong>Waist - </strong>Measure across the navel.<br></p><p><strong>Hips (female only) - </strong>measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.<br></p><p><br></p><p>I recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. If you use this method, then hang on to the measurements you get and we'll use them in the next module.</p><p><br></p><p>While you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with...<br></p>","text":"The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and a calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.\nAll your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:\n\nNeck - Measure at the base of your neck.\nWaist - Measure across the navel.\nHips (female only) - measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.\n\nI recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. If you use this method, then hang on to the measurements you get and we'll use them in the next module.\nWhile you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Option Three — The Visual Method","html":"<p><em>Option Three — The Visual Method</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate.</p><p><br></p><p>\t<strong>1.\tTake a clear full-body photo of yourself. </strong>Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo.<br><br></p><p><strong>2.\tCompare it to a body fat percentage chart. </strong>Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts.<br><br></p><p><strong>3.\tLook at key areas. </strong>Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different.<br><br></p><p><strong>4. Find your match.</strong> Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution.</p><p><br></p><p>And once you've got an estimated bodyfat, we're good to proceed.</p>","text":"This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate.\n\t1.\tTake a clear full-body photo of yourself. Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo.\n\n2.\tCompare it to a body fat percentage chart. Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts.\n\n3.\tLook at key areas. Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different.\n\n4. Find your match. Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution.\nAnd once you've got an estimated bodyfat, we're good to proceed."}]}]},{"id":"playing-on-expert-mode","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985116520-e40780cdcc2bc8e4a282bab11d31c29d5d0af800053199120ac76b588a8376d0-d_1280x720?region=us","n":8,"title":"Playing on expert mode.","m":1,"vimeo":"1058525128","dur":28,"code":"0204","draft":true,"lifted":["HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","Playing on expert mode."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"By now, you know <em>exactly how to calculate </em>on <strong>expert mode.</strong><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>So, it's time to put those skills to work.<strong><br></strong></p>","text":"By now, you know exactly how to calculate on expert mode.\nSo, it's time to put those skills to work."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058525128","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058525128?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Calculating your macros.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Calculating your macros.<br></p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"Crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros.","text":"Crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros."},{"type":"text","html":"<strong><em>Option One </em></strong>— <strong><em>Your native app.</em></strong>","text":"Option One — Your native app."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it. Follow the instructions it provides, and it'll update your targets.<br><br></p><p>Don't allow your app to split your macros by percentage. Make sure you have gram values to work from, or use a different calculation method.</p>","text":"Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it. Follow the instructions it provides, and it'll update your targets.\n\nDon't allow your app to split your macros by percentage. Make sure you have gram values to work from, or use a different calculation method."},{"type":"text","html":"<strong><em>Option Two </em></strong>— <strong><em>An online calculator.</em></strong>","text":"Option Two — An online calculator."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>For a macro calculator I trust, go to <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/macros\">https://bthr.rodeo/macros</a><br><br>Under the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat.</p><p><br></p><p>Once you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move.</p>","text":"For a macro calculator I trust, go to https://bthr.rodeo/macros\n\nUnder the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat.\nOnce you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move."},{"type":"text","html":"<strong><em>Option Three </em></strong>— <strong><em>The INMRS Toolkit</em></strong>","text":"Option Three — The INMRS Toolkit"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>For more control over your diet setup and preferences, you can use the INMRS calculator below.</p><p><br></p><p>It'll walk you through the process of going from measurements to tailored macros, including calculating your bodyfat, adjusting for your goal, and fine tuning your macros based on your goals needs and personal preferences.</p>","text":"For more control over your diet setup and preferences, you can use the INMRS calculator below.\nIt'll walk you through the process of going from measurements to tailored macros, including calculating your bodyfat, adjusting for your goal, and fine tuning your macros based on your goals needs and personal preferences."},{"type":"download","title":"The INMRS Toolkit","sub":"This is a view-only file. You'll need to duplicate it to save an editable copy for yourself.","button":"DOWNLOAD","href":"https://bthr.rodeo/inmrs/toolkit","toolkit":1}]}]},{"id":"this-sections-secrets","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985117844-3228d6b864ef5ca53b589f8d0cd4139b7806b140eeb435e599e6b39456233109-d_1280x720?region=us","n":9,"title":"This section's secrets.","m":1,"vimeo":"1058525408","dur":47,"code":"0205","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES","This section's secrets."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"And <em>just like that... </em>you now know EVERYTHING you need for starting with a pro level foundation.<br>","text":"And just like that... you now know EVERYTHING you need for starting with a pro level foundation."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058525408","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058525408?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Here's this section's upgrades...","html":"<p>Here's this section's upgrades...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<strong>1. Calculators are NOT the be-all, end-all! </strong>Sure, they're a decent place to start. But <u>do not take them as gospel</u> for your goals. Do that, and you'll screw yourself over from the start.<br><br><p><strong>2. Calories and protein are KING. </strong>Maybe you knew that, maybe you didn't. But remember the other side of that coin: it means that <em>everything else pales in comparison</em> for achieving your goal. And now you know why...<br><br></p><p><strong>3. You MUST have your percentage locked in to win. </strong>It doesn't have to be perfect (in the ballpark is fine). As long as we've got a decent estimate, we'll skyrocket the chances of success from the get go.<br><br></p><p>That's this section's secrets. And I'd be lying if I said this section wasn't a total zzzZZZzZzZzzz-fest compared to what we're about to cover next.</p> <p><strong>In the next one, I'm about to rock your world and get you <u>eating </u></strong><em><strong><u>good </u></strong></em><strong><u>to get jacked.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Let's do it!</p>","text":"1. Calculators are NOT the be-all, end-all! Sure, they're a decent place to start. But do not take them as gospel for your goals. Do that, and you'll screw yourself over from the start.\n\n2. Calories and protein are KING. Maybe you knew that, maybe you didn't. But remember the other side of that coin: it means that everything else pales in comparison for achieving your goal. And now you know why...\n\n3. You MUST have your percentage locked in to win. It doesn't have to be perfect (in the ballpark is fine). As long as we've got a decent estimate, we'll skyrocket the chances of success from the get go.\n\nThat's this section's secrets. And I'd be lying if I said this section wasn't a total zzzZZZzZzZzzz-fest compared to what we're about to cover next. In the next one, I'm about to rock your world and get you eating good to get jacked.\nLet's do it!"}]},{"id":"this-is-the-end-of-crash-diets","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985118369-d844555ee4412e42ab72ac3d218e8bde303300c38de9bfec0dcb5de2b0c8bef1-d_1280x720?region=us","n":10,"title":"This is the end of crash diets.","m":2,"vimeo":"1058525881","dur":49,"code":"0301","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","This is the end of crash diets."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"You're about to get handed the keys to building your own, fully customised menu so you...","text":"You're about to get handed the keys to building your own, fully customised menu so you..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Never have to eat another crash diet again!","html":"<p>Never have to eat another crash diet again!</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"In this section, you're about to make BS, restrictive diets that never last <em>a thing of the past. </em>We're going to cover...<p><em><br></em></p><ul><li> <strong>The It's Not Macro-cket Science method </strong>for making <u>your own diet</u>, completely from scratch...<br><br></li><li><strong>How to make food you actually wanna eat </strong>the food that gets you <em>jacked...<br></em><br></li><li><strong><em>Exactly </em>what to focus on <em></em></strong>and <em>exactly what order </em>to focus on it for elite level results...<br><br></li><li><strong>And how to deal with </strong>the \"<em>I know what to do, but I just don't stick to it!\" </em>problem.</li></ul><p></p><p><br></p><p>Let’s do it!</p>","text":"In this section, you're about to make BS, restrictive diets that never last a thing of the past. We're going to cover...\n The It's Not Macro-cket Science method for making your own diet, completely from scratch...\n\nHow to make food you actually wanna eat the food that gets you jacked...\n\nExactly what to focus on and exactly what order to focus on it for elite level results...\n\nAnd how to deal with the \"I know what to do, but I just don't stick to it!\" problem.\nLet’s do it!"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058525881","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058525881?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"the-big-rocks-budget","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985118613-faa666c359a7ecda57f3da3d076b567dc20b30f9cca3ff4a4d45e2cd963453e4-d_1280x720?region=us","n":11,"title":"The 'big rocks' budget.","m":2,"vimeo":"1058526300","dur":210,"code":"0302","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","The 'big rocks' budget."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Do the right work, and you'll do well. But...","text":"Do the right work, and you'll do well. But..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Do the right work in the right order, and you'll win.","html":"<p>Do the right work in the right order, and <u>you'll win.</u></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>In this module, we break down the budget idea behind It's Not Macro-cket Science.<br></p><p><br></p><p>It’s how we make sure we’re addressing the big rocks first, and making sure <em>we don’t do what doesn’t count</em> until we’re on track to win.</p>","text":"In this module, we break down the budget idea behind It's Not Macro-cket Science.\n\nIt’s how we make sure we’re addressing the big rocks first, and making sure we don’t do what doesn’t count until we’re on track to win."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058526300","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058526300?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"how-to-eat-whatever-the-hell-you-want-and-get-jacked-doing-it","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985119079-ba7773a0cbe091430cf7003aae06bd6aaf3ad5307d589f1512ceb24b6c2bc6c6-d_1280x720?region=us","n":12,"title":"How to eat whatever the hell you want (and get jacked doing it).","m":2,"vimeo":"1058528194","dur":308,"code":"0303","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","How to eat whatever the hell you want (and get jacked doing it)."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"What else do you want me to say?<p><br></p><p><strong>I think the title speaks for itself. </strong></p><p><br></p><p><em>Shall we?</em> 😏</p>","text":"What else do you want me to say?\nI think the title speaks for itself. \nShall we? 😏"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058528194","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058528194?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — The Wish List Menu.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — The Wish List Menu.<br></p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"Here's how to put together your Wish List Menu.","text":"Here's how to put together your Wish List Menu."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.","html":"<p><em>Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page.</p><p><br></p><p>Giving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓</p>","text":"Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page.\nGiving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.","html":"<p><em>Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on.","text":"Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Write out the menu.","html":"<p><em>Step Three — Write out the menu.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>And remember that <em>the only criteria </em>you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?</p><p><br></p><p>Don't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Start by naming what you're eating. </strong>Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch.</p><p><strong>2.\tWrite out each ingredient. </strong>Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on.</p><p><strong>3.\tInclude the details. </strong>Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.</p><p><br></p><p>But again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there.</p>","text":"And remember that the only criteria you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?\nDon't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.\n1. Start by naming what you're eating. Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch.2.\tWrite out each ingredient. Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on.3.\tInclude the details. Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.\nBut again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there."}]}]},{"id":"this-might-piss-you-off","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985119768-32e8002631250d3c6a1418e659de4f26137c7cff6f78496ba408beb1efbcbf10-d_1280x720?region=us","n":13,"title":"This might piss you off.","m":2,"vimeo":"1058531968","dur":168,"code":"0304","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","This might piss you off."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Don't get mad at me, though! I'm just the one telling you...","text":"Don't get mad at me, though! I'm just the one telling you..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"There's a better way.","html":"<p>There's a better way.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"The usual methods of using macros are <em>doghouse.</em><em><br></em><p>It's Not Macro-cket Science uses a tiny (but <u>powerful)</u> pivot on the usual approach. It's so simple it might <em>piss you off </em>for not having thought of it, and it'll make menu building <em>so much more</em> simple and effective.</p>","text":"The usual methods of using macros are doghouse.\nIt's Not Macro-cket Science uses a tiny (but powerful) pivot on the usual approach. It's so simple it might piss you off for not having thought of it, and it'll make menu building so much more simple and effective."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058531968","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058531968?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"your-wish-list-menu-depends-on-this","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985120263-e6279465026947bf555db6addb2fdcea267e4fdbc7bcd9bf7f8c7482fefe60cf-d_1280x720?region=us","n":14,"title":"Your wish list menu depends on this.","m":2,"vimeo":"1058534014","dur":244,"code":"0305","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","Your wish list menu depends on this."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>To put it all together and <em>make it work, </em>you'll need...<br></p>","text":"To put it all together and make it work, you'll need..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The priorities and the pro-level mindset.","html":"<p>The priorities and the pro-level mindset.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>These are your fast-track to upgrading the way you think to Top Doggie status and start thinking how I think when I'm building menus.</p>","text":"These are your fast-track to upgrading the way you think to Top Doggie status and start thinking how I think when I'm building menus."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058534014","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058534014?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"text","html":"We've covered the priorities for a cut in the video, but let's do a walkthrough on both sides of dieting and how our focus shifts slightly depending on the goal.<p><br></p><p>To remind you: either way you slice it, we're dieting to create change. The body's not a huge fan of it, and it'll hit back at us. But how that looks depends on what kind of stress we're imposing when we diet.<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"We've covered the priorities for a cut in the video, but let's do a walkthrough on both sides of dieting and how our focus shifts slightly depending on the goal.\nTo remind you: either way you slice it, we're dieting to create change. The body's not a huge fan of it, and it'll hit back at us. But how that looks depends on what kind of stress we're imposing when we diet."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>⚠️</p><p><br></p><p><strong>If you've been viewing on mobile, please switch to desktop now. </strong></p><p><br></p><p>This module's formatting doesn't hold up on mobile, and you won't be able to make sense of the information without switching.</p><p><br></p>","text":"⚠️\nIf you've been viewing on mobile, please switch to desktop now. \nThis module's formatting doesn't hold up on mobile, and you won't be able to make sense of the information without switching.","desk":1},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Cutting","html":"<p><br>Cutting</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"Fat loss is, generally speaking, not fun. Your body's far more inclined to give you a hard time in how it responds, so let's look at what to expect and how we approach it.","text":"Fat loss is, generally speaking, not fun. Your body's far more inclined to give you a hard time in how it responds, so let's look at what to expect and how we approach it."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"HOW A CUT PHASE WORKS","html":"<p><em>HOW A CUT PHASE WORKS</em></p>"},{"type":"columns","layout":"two","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we want</strong><br></p>","text":"What we want"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we do</strong><br></p>","text":"What we do"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we get</strong><br></p>","text":"What we get"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Drop bodyfat and keep sexy muscle 😏</p>","text":"Drop bodyfat and keep sexy muscle 😏"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Create a deficit of energy through dropping food, or boosting activity, or a mix of both.</p>","text":"Create a deficit of energy through dropping food, or boosting activity, or a mix of both."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Uh, strap in...<br></p><p><br></p><p>Increases in hunger, food focus and food reward to drive additional energy consumption.<br></p><p>Drops in workout performance and general energy to inhibit burning of fuel.</p><p>Potential muscle loss due to increased protein breakdown for energy.</p><p>Decreases in immune function and production of important hormones.</p><p>More difficulty getting nutrients in due to a smaller budget to do so.</p>","text":"Uh, strap in...\n\nIncreases in hunger, food focus and food reward to drive additional energy consumption.\nDrops in workout performance and general energy to inhibit burning of fuel.Potential muscle loss due to increased protein breakdown for energy.Decreases in immune function and production of important hormones.More difficulty getting nutrients in due to a smaller budget to do so."}],[],[]]}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>All in all, not a stack of fun. Done right, we'll get what we want but we have a couple of symptoms to contend with on the way there. We're looking at a bunch of different mechanisms to try and bring back energy balance. It's the body finding a way to roadblock fat loss in an effort to keep you safe.</p><p><br></p><p>But that's also what helps inform our priorities when we cut. Knowing all this, we can intelligently structure our approach.</p><p><br></p>","text":"All in all, not a stack of fun. Done right, we'll get what we want but we have a couple of symptoms to contend with on the way there. We're looking at a bunch of different mechanisms to try and bring back energy balance. It's the body finding a way to roadblock fat loss in an effort to keep you safe.\nBut that's also what helps inform our priorities when we cut. Knowing all this, we can intelligently structure our approach."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"THE CUTTING PRIORITY PYRAMID","html":"<p><em>THE CUTTING PRIORITY PYRAMID<br></em></p>"},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fcut-1739781083.png","file":"cut-1739781083.png","alt":"","route":"pyramid-cut"},{"type":"columns","layout":"two","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Pro mindset</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Pro mindset"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Protein</strong><br></p>","text":"Protein"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Fat</strong><br></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Fat"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong> Carbohydrate</strong><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Carbohydrate"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong> Fun</strong></p>","text":"Fun"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Staying inside calories and eating foods that are satiating, go the distance, digest slowly, and keep you happy (but not too happy).</p>","text":"Staying inside calories and eating foods that are satiating, go the distance, digest slowly, and keep you happy (but not too happy)."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Helps repair tissues and prevents muscle losses so you don't end up skinny, and helps keeps you full.</p>","text":"Helps repair tissues and prevents muscle losses so you don't end up skinny, and helps keeps you full."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Supports hormone production, brain and joint health and vitamin absorption so you stay healthy, plus helps control appetite by increasing your sense of fullness and stabilising blood sugar. Absolutely essential for health and not dying.</p>","text":"Supports hormone production, brain and joint health and vitamin absorption so you stay healthy, plus helps control appetite by increasing your sense of fullness and stabilising blood sugar. Absolutely essential for health and not dying."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Fuels workouts so you can train to preserve (or even grow) muscle, helps protect it by sparing protein, and supports brain function, mood regulation and energy levels. Really damn good for ya, but just not something you'll die without.</p>","text":"Fuels workouts so you can train to preserve (or even grow) muscle, helps protect it by sparing protein, and supports brain function, mood regulation and energy levels. Really damn good for ya, but just not something you'll die without."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Means you can eat Chokito bars and other yum stuff that makes your diet human friendly and balanced.</p>","text":"Means you can eat Chokito bars and other yum stuff that makes your diet human friendly and balanced."}],[],[]]}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>By organising our approach this way, we get to tick off the things we need for success and optimise our diet build to help manage the challenges that come part and parcel of a fat loss approach.</p><p><br></p><p>Addressing each of the priorities with the pro mindset will help further refine the approach so it's ideal both in the big structure, and the finer details of execution.<br></p>","text":"By organising our approach this way, we get to tick off the things we need for success and optimise our diet build to help manage the challenges that come part and parcel of a fat loss approach.\nAddressing each of the priorities with the pro mindset will help further refine the approach so it's ideal both in the big structure, and the finer details of execution."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Gaining","html":"<p><br>Gaining</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Gaining is a whole lot more fun for the body. It's rich in resources, well fuelled and in the right circumstances to thrive. But even so, any consistent exposure to something that disrupts the body's baseline will end up creating pushback.</p>","text":"Gaining is a whole lot more fun for the body. It's rich in resources, well fuelled and in the right circumstances to thrive. But even so, any consistent exposure to something that disrupts the body's baseline will end up creating pushback."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"HOW A GAIN PHASE WORKS","html":"<p><em>HOW A GAIN PHASE WORKS<br></em></p>"},{"type":"columns","layout":"two","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we want</strong><br></p>","text":"What we want"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we do</strong><br></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"What we do"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>What we get</strong><br></p>","text":"What we get"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>More sexy muscle and minimal gain in bodyfat.<br></p>","text":"More sexy muscle and minimal gain in bodyfat."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Create a surplus of energy through food, and use a well designed resistance program (Forge, for example...) to trigger muscle growth and direct the additional resources to it.<br></p>","text":"Create a surplus of energy through food, and use a well designed resistance program (Forge, for example...) to trigger muscle growth and direct the additional resources to it."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Downturn in appetite and food focus to make sustaining the surplus harder.<br></p><p>Increases in metabolism that expend additional calories.</p><p>Altered nutrient partitioning that preferentially stores extra intake as fat.</p><p>Digestive issues due to gross volume of extra food consumed.</p>","text":"Downturn in appetite and food focus to make sustaining the surplus harder.\nIncreases in metabolism that expend additional calories.Altered nutrient partitioning that preferentially stores extra intake as fat.Digestive issues due to gross volume of extra food consumed."}],[],[]]}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>For someone coming from a fat loss background, it's definitely more favourable a set of symptoms. But when the goal's muscle gain and you rely on consistently eating enough to drive your gains, having your body interfere with that or racking up extra fat mass as you try and grow is its own unique kind of 'not fun'.<br></p><p><br></p><p>And again, that knowledge informs our priorities and mindset. So, here's how we intelligently tackle structuring a gaining diet.</p><p><br></p>","text":"For someone coming from a fat loss background, it's definitely more favourable a set of symptoms. But when the goal's muscle gain and you rely on consistently eating enough to drive your gains, having your body interfere with that or racking up extra fat mass as you try and grow is its own unique kind of 'not fun'.\n\nAnd again, that knowledge informs our priorities and mindset. So, here's how we intelligently tackle structuring a gaining diet."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"THE GAINING PRIORITY PYRAMID","html":"<p><em>THE GAINING PRIORITY PYRAMID<br></em></p>"},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fgain-1739781118.png","file":"gain-1739781118.png","alt":"","route":"pyramid-gain"},{"type":"columns","layout":"two","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Pro mindset</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Pro mindset"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Protein</strong><br></p>","text":"Protein"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Carbohydrate</strong><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Carbohydrate"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Fat</strong><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Fat"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Fun</strong><br></p>","text":"Fun"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Hitting calorie targets and eating foods that are not too satiating, easy to consume and digest, and tolerable in high volumes.<br></p>","text":"Hitting calorie targets and eating foods that are not too satiating, easy to consume and digest, and tolerable in high volumes."},{"type":"text","html":"<p> Helps repair and grow new muscle tissue and respond positively to training.<br></p>","text":"Helps repair and grow new muscle tissue and respond positively to training."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Fuels intense workings, replenishes the body's carb stores for future workouts, spikes insulin to shuttle nutrients into muscles, and keeps you from burning protein for energy, and makes it easier to train hard and build muscle with minimal fat gain. Aim for low fibre, easily digested carb sources.<br></p>","text":"Fuels intense workings, replenishes the body's carb stores for future workouts, spikes insulin to shuttle nutrients into muscles, and keeps you from burning protein for energy, and makes it easier to train hard and build muscle with minimal fat gain. Aim for low fibre, easily digested carb sources."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Supports hormone production for a good response to training, helps absorb vitamins and nutrients, helps to get calories in efficiently and makes food easier and more palatable to eat. But has to be moderated or excess fat gain can happen.<br></p>","text":"Supports hormone production for a good response to training, helps absorb vitamins and nutrients, helps to get calories in efficiently and makes food easier and more palatable to eat. But has to be moderated or excess fat gain can happen."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>For the same reasons, and likely with a slightly larger available budget. A good approach is to have fun baked in to the rest of your priorities.<br></p>","text":"For the same reasons, and likely with a slightly larger available budget. A good approach is to have fun baked in to the rest of your priorities."}],[],[]]}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>In terms of priorities, the changes in a gaining approach are minor. But the shift in mindset has a really significant impact. How you execute each of these priorities will make a big difference in how easy your diet is to execute.<br></p><p><br></p><p>In the next module, we'll start putting all of this to work.<br></p>","text":"In terms of priorities, the changes in a gaining approach are minor. But the shift in mindset has a really significant impact. How you execute each of these priorities will make a big difference in how easy your diet is to execute.\n\nIn the next module, we'll start putting all of this to work."}]},{"id":"the-exact-step-by-step-process","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985120722-58257694902bb00aaa7478b7315b4a2cbe428907f6f628a0616896e6c9fec603-d_1280x720?region=us","n":15,"title":"The exact, step-by-step process.","m":2,"vimeo":"1058539908","dur":281,"code":"0306","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","The exact, step-by-step process."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Once you've finished this step, you'll have done it. In your hands, ready to use...","text":"Once you've finished this step, you'll have done it. In your hands, ready to use..."},{"type":"text","html":"<strong>Your very first It's Not Macro-cket Science menu 🥳</strong>","text":"Your very first It's Not Macro-cket Science menu 🥳"},{"type":"text","html":"And it'll just get better from here.","text":"And it'll just get better from here."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058539908","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058539908?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Alright, let's run through that below with a step-by-step.</p>","text":"Alright, let's run through that below with a step-by-step."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Building your menu.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Building your menu.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.<p><br></p><p>But before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities.</p><p><br></p>","text":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.\nBut before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Identify your first priority.","html":"<p><em>Step One — Identify your first priority.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now.<p><br></p>","text":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Track it.","html":"<p><em>Step Two — Track it.</em></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.<br><p>If you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that.</p><p><br></p><p>At the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range.<br></p><p><br></p><p>Don't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.\nIf you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that.\nAt the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range.\n\nDon't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Rinse and repeat.","html":"<p><em>Step Three — Rinse and repeat.</em><em></em></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.</p><p><br></p><p>And that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu.</p>","text":"Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.\nAnd that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu."}]}]},{"id":"this-sections-secrets-1","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985121228-f3b4644f80845d5b91865fca256941346f5738c9fea1f0ff150e78355008c722-d_1280x720?region=us","n":16,"title":"This section's secrets...","m":2,"vimeo":"1058543032","dur":33,"code":"0307","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT WHAT YOU WANT","This section's secrets."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"With that, you've got all the tools for the build.","text":"With that, you've got all the tools for the build."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058543032","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058543032?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Here's what you just learned...","html":"<p>Here's what you just learned...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>1. The 'big rocks' budget </strong>is how we get you locked in with the needle movers <em>first, </em>and how we use the Three Laws to make it all work.</p><br><p><strong>2. You can <em>and <u>should</u></em> eat whatever the hell you want. </strong>And if you work with the right priorities, you can use it to put together a menu that gets you jacked.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. The pro mindset </strong>will skip you years ahead with menu building, get you thinking like an expert, show you how to think about 'eating right' for YOU, and get you <em>jacked.</em></p><p><br></p><p> In the next section, you're about to find out that all of that <u>could be for NOTHING</u> if you make the mistakes I'll show you.<br></p><p><br></p><p>Get straight to it!</p>","text":"1. The 'big rocks' budget is how we get you locked in with the needle movers first, and how we use the Three Laws to make it all work.\n2. You can and should eat whatever the hell you want. And if you work with the right priorities, you can use it to put together a menu that gets you jacked.\n3. The pro mindset will skip you years ahead with menu building, get you thinking like an expert, show you how to think about 'eating right' for YOU, and get you jacked.\n In the next section, you're about to find out that all of that could be for NOTHING if you make the mistakes I'll show you.\n\nGet straight to it!"}]},{"id":"skip-this-to-screw-up-all-your-work","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985124310-97206aa79dbbae5881a51ebcba46ca2e16bf4b3d4b643b625df89dde26c91ec1-d_1280x720?region=us","n":17,"title":"Skip this to screw up all your work.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058543560","dur":56,"code":"0401","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","Skip this to screw up all your work."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>It sucks, but it's true...<br></p>","text":"It sucks, but it's true..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"If you don't know how to track right, everything you've done will be worth jack 😮‍💨","html":"<p>If you don't know how to <u>track right</u>, everything you've done will be worth <em>jack </em>😮‍💨</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"In this section, you'll find out how to <u>get what you deserve</u> for the work you put in. Don't rip yourself off. We're going to cover...","text":"In this section, you'll find out how to get what you deserve for the work you put in. Don't rip yourself off. We're going to cover..."},{"type":"text","html":"<ul><li><strong>The nightmare scenario</strong> that could <em>spell the death</em> of your macro tracking journey...<br><br></li><li><strong>My shortlist of exactly what to do</strong> and <em>what not to do</em> to make sure you succeed...<br><br></li><li><strong>The </strong><em><strong>most common mistakes</strong></em><strong> I see, </strong>so you can spot them faster and get away from them sooner...<br><br></li><li><strong>And a little hippy take</strong> that’ll shift your perspective and kick you up a gear with course correcting.<br></li></ul><p></p><p><br></p><p>Let’s do it!</p>","text":"The nightmare scenario that could spell the death of your macro tracking journey...\n\nMy shortlist of exactly what to do and what not to do to make sure you succeed...\n\nThe most common mistakes I see, so you can spot them faster and get away from them sooner...\n\nAnd a little hippy take that’ll shift your perspective and kick you up a gear with course correcting.\n\nLet’s do it!"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058543560","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058543560?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"exactly-how-not-to-track","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985122873-c266f02c17d3ffabc77ea9556e4784bde72cdbbd2b882bd46f19edb0517b4fa0-d_1280x720?region=us","n":18,"title":"Exactly how NOT to track.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058544154","dur":261,"code":"0402","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","Exactly how NOT to track."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>I could go on for days about all the little things you can do to track right. But how about this...<br></p>","text":"I could go on for days about all the little things you can do to track right. But how about this..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Let me give you a one-line definition for what NOT to do... 🙃","html":"<p>Let me give you a one-line definition for <em>what NOT to do... </em>🙃</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>I'll get to my pro-tips once I've finished making myself look like an idiot below.</p>","text":"I'll get to my pro-tips once I've finished making myself look like an idiot below."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058544154","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058544154?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"how-i-do-things-after-10-years","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985122991-0aad72efeb7ae432abe1312fd8414446ec9a7d4a11c027d7177d6509deae08d5-d_1280x720?region=us","n":19,"title":"How I do things after 10+ years.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058547074","dur":69,"code":"0403","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","How I do things after 10+ years."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>I've been doing this a while, and tracking is a piece of cake. But...<br></p>","text":"I've been doing this a while, and tracking is a piece of cake. But..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"I would be lying to you if I said it started that way.","html":"<p>I would be <em>lying to you </em>if I said it started that way.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>When you're new, this part of the process is a <u>giant headache</u>. The sooner you learn these simple protocols, that faster you'll get to 'piece of cake' territory.</p>","text":"When you're new, this part of the process is a giant headache. The sooner you learn these simple protocols, that faster you'll get to 'piece of cake' territory."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058547074","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058547074?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Easy and simple food tracking? This is the ONLY WAY I do it.","html":"<p><br>Easy and simple food tracking? This is the <u>ONLY WAY</u> I do it.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>When it comes to doing a good job of tracking what we eat, we're after accuracy, consistency and simplicity. We need to make sure we're minding the details, we're doing it all the time, and we're making it as easy and low friction as we can.</p><p><br></p><p>These protocols should be baked into your approach if you want an easy time doing it.</p>","text":"When it comes to doing a good job of tracking what we eat, we're after accuracy, consistency and simplicity. We need to make sure we're minding the details, we're doing it all the time, and we're making it as easy and low friction as we can.\nThese protocols should be baked into your approach if you want an easy time doing it."},{"type":"faq","items":[{"q":"Measure by weight, not by volume.","html":"Doing anything other than measuring by weight will 10x your chances of inaccuracy. A flat scoop versus mounded, compacted versus loosely packed, a tablespoon measure versus a tablespoon and so on are all really obvious examples of how much variation you can have if you aren't using weight as your metric.<br><br>\nMeasuring (and I recommend by grams) is the most consistent and reliable way to track, and I do not ever use any other method. Neither should you 😘","text":"Doing anything other than measuring by weight will 10x your chances of inaccuracy. A flat scoop versus mounded, compacted versus loosely packed, a tablespoon measure versus a tablespoon and so on are all really obvious examples of how much variation you can have if you aren't using weight as your metric.\n\n\nMeasuring (and I recommend by grams) is the most consistent and reliable way to track, and I do not ever use any other method. Neither should you 😘"},{"q":"Measure raw, not cooked.","html":"Boil a potato versus bake it, and you're adding moisture instead of taking it away. You'll get less calories for the same cooked weight boiled, and more if it's baked. Cook one chicken thigh for ten minutes, and another for twelve, and they'll come out different. The one that's lost more water will have more calories per cooked gram. Add more water to your oats, and per cooked portion, they'll be lower in calories than if you cooked them with less.<br><br>\nOr, you could just weigh all your ingredients before you cook them, and not have to worry about it 😎","text":"Boil a potato versus bake it, and you're adding moisture instead of taking it away. You'll get less calories for the same cooked weight boiled, and more if it's baked. Cook one chicken thigh for ten minutes, and another for twelve, and they'll come out different. The one that's lost more water will have more calories per cooked gram. Add more water to your oats, and per cooked portion, they'll be lower in calories than if you cooked them with less.\n\n\nOr, you could just weigh all your ingredients before you cook them, and not have to worry about it 😎"},{"q":"Subtract, don't add.","html":"I would absolutely lose my mind if I had to scoop and rescoop little spoons of peanut butter until I hit the 15g I wanted, or to weigh out my olive oil in a little bowl before putting it in my pan.<br><br>\nThankfully, I'm still sane (and tracking accurately) because the tare feature exists. It's far easier to subtract from the container by zeroing the scale before using than it is to weigh out tiny portions of things. If you want a smoother time, do that.","text":"I would absolutely lose my mind if I had to scoop and rescoop little spoons of peanut butter until I hit the 15g I wanted, or to weigh out my olive oil in a little bowl before putting it in my pan.\n\n\nThankfully, I'm still sane (and tracking accurately) because the tare feature exists. It's far easier to subtract from the container by zeroing the scale before using than it is to weigh out tiny portions of things. If you want a smoother time, do that."},{"q":"Use microscales.","html":"The bigger the scale and the higher its capacity, the less accurate it tends to be with small portions. A good set of microscales (like the ones I recommend) are accurate from 0.1g to 3000g, and they're a good choice for making sure things like cooking oils and energy dense things are measured accurately and easily.","text":"The bigger the scale and the higher its capacity, the less accurate it tends to be with small portions. A good set of microscales (like the ones I recommend) are accurate from 0.1g to 3000g, and they're a good choice for making sure things like cooking oils and energy dense things are measured accurately and easily."},{"q":"Measure big, and then eyeball.","html":"I used to weigh every ingredient when I cooked a batch of something, and then I'd weigh out every portion once it was done. If you're just cooking for you, that's double handling that you don't need to worry about.<br><br>\nInstead, just weigh things when you cook and eyeball it into however many portions you cooked. It won't be perfect, but the numbers all shake out the same at the end of the week and it's far easier to do.","text":"I used to weigh every ingredient when I cooked a batch of something, and then I'd weigh out every portion once it was done. If you're just cooking for you, that's double handling that you don't need to worry about.\n\n\nInstead, just weigh things when you cook and eyeball it into however many portions you cooked. It won't be perfect, but the numbers all shake out the same at the end of the week and it's far easier to do."},{"q":"Make your app do the heavy lifting.","html":"A good tracking app has a bunch of different features to do the work for you. From things like saving groups of ingredients as meals or recipes, to copying and pasting repeat meals and so on, there are plenty of things your app can handle for you.<br><br>\nIt is an extremely good idea to spend some time learning what different features your app has. You're interacting with it every day, but how you do so will depend a great deal on how good you are at using it. My advice? Same deal as our flywheel, do the work up front and get the thing spinning fast so it takes minimal effort in the future.","text":"A good tracking app has a bunch of different features to do the work for you. From things like saving groups of ingredients as meals or recipes, to copying and pasting repeat meals and so on, there are plenty of things your app can handle for you.\n\n\nIt is an extremely good idea to spend some time learning what different features your app has. You're interacting with it every day, but how you do so will depend a great deal on how good you are at using it. My advice? Same deal as our flywheel, do the work up front and get the thing spinning fast so it takes minimal effort in the future."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Tracking you is always done like this...","html":"<p><br>Tracking you is <em>always </em>done like this...</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Then, there's you. We've got to keep eyes on what's happening with your body as it responds to the diet so we can make sure things are working effectively. To track you correctly, you'll need to:</p><p><br></p><p></p><ul><li><strong>Weigh dry. </strong>After you've been to the bathroom, and before you eat anything.<strong><br><br></strong></li><li><strong>Weigh naked. </strong>That, or in the same clothing each time.<strong><br><br></strong></li><li><strong>Weigh at the same time. </strong>Usually, that's first thing in the morning and at around the same time each day.<strong><br><br></strong></li><li><strong>Weigh consistently. </strong>The more frequently you weigh in under these conditions, the better informed we are about what's going on.</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Beyond this, taking body measurements is a great idea if you have someone to assist you. If you don't, I find they're too hard to do accurately and not really worth the effort. </p><p><br></p><p>If you're interested in the numbers and have the resources, like we covered in an earlier section, getting DEXA scans on a regular basis is a great way to collect very useable data to get an accurate picture of your progress over time.</p><p></p>","text":"Then, there's you. We've got to keep eyes on what's happening with your body as it responds to the diet so we can make sure things are working effectively. To track you correctly, you'll need to:\nWeigh dry. After you've been to the bathroom, and before you eat anything.\n\nWeigh naked. That, or in the same clothing each time.\n\nWeigh at the same time. Usually, that's first thing in the morning and at around the same time each day.\n\nWeigh consistently. The more frequently you weigh in under these conditions, the better informed we are about what's going on.\nBeyond this, taking body measurements is a great idea if you have someone to assist you. If you don't, I find they're too hard to do accurately and not really worth the effort. \nIf you're interested in the numbers and have the resources, like we covered in an earlier section, getting DEXA scans on a regular basis is a great way to collect very useable data to get an accurate picture of your progress over time."}]},{"id":"everyone-is-doing-this-stuff-wrong","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985123702-1a8391aa06ed1f5c7eb82dc7be2aec1dbced7c6ff59831aad48121206a25e9d2-d_1280x720?region=us","n":20,"title":"EVERYONE is doing this stuff wrong.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058547808","dur":105,"code":"0404","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","EVERYONE is doing this stuff wrong."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>This is the stuff that <em>every tracker <u>screws up</u></em>. And here's the thing...</p>","text":"This is the stuff that every tracker screws up. And here's the thing..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"I do not care if you do it too 😏","html":"<p>I <u>do not care</u> if you do it too 😏 </p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Because what you're <em>really </em><em>aiming for? </em>That's what we're gonna cover in this video.</p>","text":"Because what you're really aiming for? That's what we're gonna cover in this video."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058547808","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058547808?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Here's what you're watching for...","html":"<p><br>Here's what you're watching for...</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Remember, none of these things in isolation are a big problem. But left unidentified and unaddressed, they can be. Make mistakes, spot them fast and pivot even faster. <em>You'll be better off for it.</em></p>","text":"Remember, none of these things in isolation are a big problem. But left unidentified and unaddressed, they can be. Make mistakes, spot them fast and pivot even faster. You'll be better off for it."},{"type":"faq","items":[{"q":"Missing the little things.","html":"They say 'don't sweat the small stuff'. That's a good rule. But NOT when it comes to tracking. <br><br>\nThe little things stack up. Miss enough of them, and they're not the 'little things' any more. Better to get your app to do the lifting and stay accurate than get lazy and get no results.","text":"They say 'don't sweat the small stuff'. That's a good rule. But NOT when it comes to tracking. \n\n\nThe little things stack up. Miss enough of them, and they're not the 'little things' any more. Better to get your app to do the lifting and stay accurate than get lazy and get no results."},{"q":"Tracking meals, not ingredients.","html":"I don't know how you make your lasagne. But I'll bet my bottom dollar it's not the same as how I make mine.<br><br>\nDon't search for entire meals when you're tracking something. Take the time to get each ingredient dialled in and keep your tracking tidy.","text":"I don't know how you make your lasagne. But I'll bet my bottom dollar it's not the same as how I make mine.\n\n\nDon't search for entire meals when you're tracking something. Take the time to get each ingredient dialled in and keep your tracking tidy."},{"q":"Elite level mental gymnastics","html":"I had a client that was an Olympic calibre mental gymnast. <br><br>\nHe had me stumped. For three months. We were making not one lick of progress, and I couldn't figure it out. <br><br>\nWelp, turned out the guy was doing constant mental math on how many calories the walk from his car, or the extra effort in carrying around his backpack, or a more stressful day at work was worth in snacks.<br><br>\nAnd then he was eating the snacks he'd 'earned' at night.<br><br>\nUh, don't... don't do that. Cool? Cool.","text":"I had a client that was an Olympic calibre mental gymnast. \n\n\nHe had me stumped. For three months. We were making not one lick of progress, and I couldn't figure it out. \n\n\nWelp, turned out the guy was doing constant mental math on how many calories the walk from his car, or the extra effort in carrying around his backpack, or a more stressful day at work was worth in snacks.\n\n\nAnd then he was eating the snacks he'd 'earned' at night.\n\n\nUh, don't... don't do that. Cool? Cool."},{"q":"BLTs.","html":"Bites, Licks and Tastes. This falls under the same sort of umbrella as missing the little things, but not quite.<br><br>\nOften, these happen without even really thinking about them. They're the sneaky ones to watch out for though, because they might fly under your radar, but your results will know.","text":"Bites, Licks and Tastes. This falls under the same sort of umbrella as missing the little things, but not quite.\n\n\nOften, these happen without even really thinking about them. They're the sneaky ones to watch out for though, because they might fly under your radar, but your results will know."},{"q":"Rounding like a choomba woomba.","html":"I used to never let it fly if my planned portion was 100g, and I only weighed out 95g. You better believe I fixed that up, quick. <br><br>\nBut I was never quite so fast to swing things the other way if I accidentally portioned out 105g... <br><br>\nSame thing happens in folks' tracking apps. They'll weigh out 12g of olive oil, but 10g is a nice, round number. That, and a great way to screw yourself over.","text":"I used to never let it fly if my planned portion was 100g, and I only weighed out 95g. You better believe I fixed that up, quick. \n\n\nBut I was never quite so fast to swing things the other way if I accidentally portioned out 105g... \n\n\nSame thing happens in folks' tracking apps. They'll weigh out 12g of olive oil, but 10g is a nice, round number. That, and a great way to screw yourself over."},{"q":"Always choosing the skinny options.","html":"Most apps have a database built off peer contributions. But just like the mistake above, it can be very easy to end up always choosing the leaner, lower calorie option in a bid to preserve the calories you've got left for the day.<br><br>\nCheck yourself on that. You'll make that decision once, and then repeat it any and every time you choose that food again without realising it. Dangerous.","text":"Most apps have a database built off peer contributions. But just like the mistake above, it can be very easy to end up always choosing the leaner, lower calorie option in a bid to preserve the calories you've got left for the day.\n\n\nCheck yourself on that. You'll make that decision once, and then repeat it any and every time you choose that food again without realising it. Dangerous."},{"q":"Getting cocky.","html":"NOBODY's eyeballs work as well as scales do. You might think you've got a magic knack, or a real keen eye. <br><br>\nBut don't get cocky. Use your scales.","text":"NOBODY's eyeballs work as well as scales do. You might think you've got a magic knack, or a real keen eye. \n\n\nBut don't get cocky. Use your scales."},{"q":"Fudging the data.","html":"If you have a funky weigh in, it's tempting to go, \"Nah, that doesn't seem right. I won't save that weigh in, because something's off.\" But you wouldn't do the same thing if you had a great weigh in, would ya?<br><br>\nStay consistent, and don't fudge the data.","text":"If you have a funky weigh in, it's tempting to go, \"Nah, that doesn't seem right. I won't save that weigh in, because something's off.\" But you wouldn't do the same thing if you had a great weigh in, would ya?\n\n\nStay consistent, and don't fudge the data."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>But again, remember that making these mistakes and being able to pivot away from them makes you a better tracker over time. So have a keen eye, watch for them, and get yourself back on track.</p>","text":"But again, remember that making these mistakes and being able to pivot away from them makes you a better tracker over time. So have a keen eye, watch for them, and get yourself back on track."}]},{"id":"keep-falling-off-the-wagon-watch-this","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985124102-be92d137846258f3814c4c864f8ce861efc7cd7b05a8fe2fa609cf2404990b8a-d_1280x720?region=us","n":21,"title":"Keep falling off the wagon? Watch this.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058548913","dur":161,"code":"0405","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","Keep falling off the wagon? Watch this."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Dieting ain't easy. You'll make mistakes.<br></p>","text":"Dieting ain't easy. You'll make mistakes."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>This is a </strong><u><strong>powerful mindset switch</strong></u><strong> to help keep you on track and moving forward.</strong><br></p>","text":"This is a powerful mindset switch to help keep you on track and moving forward."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>You got this thing, baby!</p>","text":"You got this thing, baby!"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058548913","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058548913?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"this-sections-secrets-2","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985124692-8ca441299599d40a39fabf0db7107e06acbeb3f5ec15d028c057a36fc9b2c9d7-d_1280x720?region=us","n":22,"title":"This section's secrets.","m":3,"vimeo":"1058550487","dur":72,"code":"0406","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS","This section's secrets."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Now you're moving like a veteran tracker 😎 see below for the refresh.","text":"Now you're moving like a veteran tracker 😎 see below for the refresh."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058550487","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058550487?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Here's this section's secrets...","html":"<p>Here's this section's secrets...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<strong>1. NOBODY starts off thinking they’ll lie to themselves.</strong> But it’s an easy trap to fall into that has so many convinced macros just ‘don’t work for them’. <em>Don’t let it be you</em>. <p><br></p><p><strong>2. Tracking right is dead simple. </strong>Be accurate, and be consistent. Ten times outta ten, I'd pick you getting your <u>tracking correct over nailing your macro targets.</u> You are ALWAYS better off that way. Don’t get them out of order. </p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. We're all doing the same stuff wrong.</strong> But the name of the game isn’t never making mistakes — it’s spotting them fast, and fixing them faster.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>4. BE CURIOUS. </strong>Figure out <u>why</u> you're being daft, <u>learn</u> from your mistakes instead of be judgy, and <u>build<em></em></u> a better, smarter approach over time. </p>","text":"1. NOBODY starts off thinking they’ll lie to themselves. But it’s an easy trap to fall into that has so many convinced macros just ‘don’t work for them’. Don’t let it be you. \n2. Tracking right is dead simple. Be accurate, and be consistent. Ten times outta ten, I'd pick you getting your tracking correct over nailing your macro targets. You are ALWAYS better off that way. Don’t get them out of order. \n3. We're all doing the same stuff wrong. But the name of the game isn’t never making mistakes — it’s spotting them fast, and fixing them faster.\n4. BE CURIOUS. Figure out why you're being daft, learn from your mistakes instead of be judgy, and build a better, smarter approach over time."}]},{"id":"were-not-here-to-lick-stamps","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985125428-576214625ba66dd5ad3d364aa0b71de2378b429d1b3f41eef84fd2867e4ea71b-d_1280x720?region=us","n":23,"title":"We're not here to lick stamps.","m":4,"vimeo":"1058551263","dur":37,"code":"0501","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","We're not here to lick stamps."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Far from it. <em>We're here to get jacked. </em>So this section is all about how to make sure you get jacked, and make it happen on YOUR timeline.<br></p><p><br></p><p>If showing you how to eat the food you love wasn't in this course... this would <u>HANDS DOWN</u> be my favourite section. It is jam-packed full of giant lessons that...</p>","text":"Far from it. We're here to get jacked. So this section is all about how to make sure you get jacked, and make it happen on YOUR timeline.\n\nIf showing you how to eat the food you love wasn't in this course... this would HANDS DOWN be my favourite section. It is jam-packed full of giant lessons that..."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><u>BLEW MY MIND</u> when I first learned them 🤯</strong></p>","text":"BLEW MY MIND when I first learned them 🤯"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>And now I'm gonna teach them to you. We're about to cover...</p>","text":"And now I'm gonna teach them to you. We're about to cover..."},{"type":"text","html":"<ul><li><strong>How to be <em>dead certain</em> you're getting jacked at the right speed </strong>and exactly what to watch for to do it...</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>The big </strong><em><strong>progress trap</strong></em> that'll get you nowhere, fast. And, how to beat it...</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Why eating boring food</strong> might actually be <em>the slickest move to make</em>...</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>The one thing that matters WAY more than what you weigh, </strong>and why you should keep your eye on it..</li></ul><p><br></p><p>And this <em>was </em>going to be a bullet, but I had to put it in header size because of how HUGE this lesson is. I'm also going to teach you my personal favourite...</p>","text":"How to be dead certain you're getting jacked at the right speed and exactly what to watch for to do it...\nThe big progress trap that'll get you nowhere, fast. And, how to beat it...\nWhy eating boring food might actually be the slickest move to make...\nThe one thing that matters WAY more than what you weigh, and why you should keep your eye on it..\nAnd this was going to be a bullet, but I had to put it in header size because of how HUGE this lesson is. I'm also going to teach you my personal favourite..."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>EXACTLY <u>HOW FAST</u> YOU CAN (AND <em>SHOULD</em>) LOSE OR GAIN WEIGHT 😍</strong></p>","text":"EXACTLY HOW FAST YOU CAN (AND SHOULD) LOSE OR GAIN WEIGHT 😍"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>I love this section. Let's go.</p>","text":"I love this section. Let's go."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058551263","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058551263?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"the-only-measure-that-really-matters","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985125648-f09652bfaaab9fbd3fdc006b7f190b35a9390351d816517c4aad3d2f7207a162-d_1280x720?region=us","n":24,"title":"The ONLY measure that really matters.","m":4,"vimeo":"1058551647","dur":160,"code":"0502","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","The ONLY measure that really matters."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>There's only <em>one thing </em>that truly counts if you want to make sure your plan is working. And it might seem simple...</p>","text":"There's only one thing that truly counts if you want to make sure your plan is working. And it might seem simple..."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>But it is a <u>GIANT trap</u> 😱</strong></p>","text":"But it is a GIANT trap 😱"},{"type":"text","html":"Not for you, though. Not once you watch this video...","text":"Not for you, though. Not once you watch this video..."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058551647","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058551647?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"stay-out-of-the-progress-trap-for-good","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985125936-e4736c249088cea74c4b5b277ac4ef7ddd3118e9d88eb77cb41ca98e00ac0888-d_1280x720?region=us","n":25,"title":"Stay OUT of the progress trap for good.","m":4,"vimeo":"1058553807","dur":168,"code":"0503","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","Stay OUT of the progress trap for good."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>I got news. This is the sure-fire formula for staying free from the progress trap.</p>","text":"I got news. This is the sure-fire formula for staying free from the progress trap."},{"type":"text","html":"<strong>This is my <u>sure-fire formula</u> for staying free from the progress trap.</strong>","text":"This is my sure-fire formula for staying free from the progress trap."},{"type":"text","html":"And now it's yours 🤓","text":"And now it's yours 🤓"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058553807","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058553807?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Getting (and staying) out of the progress trap.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Getting (and staying) out of the progress trap.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Staying out of the progress trap comes down to a pretty simple formula. It's as simple as...<br></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Staying out of the progress trap comes down to a pretty simple formula. It's as simple as..."},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fdiagram-2-1740040852.png","file":"diagram-2-1740040852.png","alt":"","route":"loop"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Once you've decided on a target rate of change, you've got a tailored-to-you metric for success. From there, you manage your execution and plan in tandem to hit that weekly or monthly target to keep yourself on track.</p><p><br></p><p>To do all this, though, you need to know what your rate is. In the next module, we'll break down your options.</p>","text":"Once you've decided on a target rate of change, you've got a tailored-to-you metric for success. From there, you manage your execution and plan in tandem to hit that weekly or monthly target to keep yourself on track.\nTo do all this, though, you need to know what your rate is. In the next module, we'll break down your options."}]}]},{"id":"just-how-fast-can-you-get-jacked","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985126307-856875f4ee6f5bf6ab3455dee4448235c0b41c9c0d6be2d8abe1a83bf82c51ca-d_1280x720?region=us","n":26,"title":"Just how fast can you get jacked?","m":4,"vimeo":"1058556549","dur":168,"code":"0504","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","Just how fast can you get jacked?"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>No word of a lie, and no exaggeration...</p>","text":"No word of a lie, and no exaggeration..."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>This is the single biggest power up that exists when it comes to dieting 📈</strong></p>","text":"This is the single biggest power up that exists when it comes to dieting 📈"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Let's break down exactly what we're aiming for here.</p>","text":"Let's break down exactly what we're aiming for here."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058556549","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058556549?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>⚠️</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>If you've been viewing on mobile, please switch to desktop now. </strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p>This module's formatting doesn't hold up on mobile, and you won't be able to make sense of the information without switching.</p><p><strong></strong><br></p>","text":"⚠️\nIf you've been viewing on mobile, please switch to desktop now. \nThis module's formatting doesn't hold up on mobile, and you won't be able to make sense of the information without switching.","desk":1},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Set your rate of progress.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Set your rate of progress.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Well, before we get to that, let's break down your options.</p><p><br></p><p>Remember, there's no one fixed rate. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Well, before we get to that, let's break down your options.\nRemember, there's no one fixed rate. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The ranges.","html":"<p><em>The ranges.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"columns","layout":"four","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>DIET SETUP</strong><br></p>","text":"DIET SETUP"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Aggressive cutting</strong><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Aggressive cutting"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>WEEKLY CHANGE</strong></p>","text":"WEEKLY CHANGE"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>1.25-2% loss<br></p>","text":"1.25-2% loss"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>FOR A 75KG PERSON</strong></p>","text":"FOR A 75KG PERSON"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>950 - 1500g loss<br></p>","text":"950 - 1500g loss"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>IDEAL CONDITIONS</strong></p>","text":"IDEAL CONDITIONS"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Suitable if you have higher bodyfat, or a very short timeline and a lot of room to take on stress. Also suited for those cleaning up bodyfat in a gaining phase. This should be used with extreme caution, and I advise against the upper end of this range unless you're working with a coach and are very high in bodyfat.<br></p>","text":"Suitable if you have higher bodyfat, or a very short timeline and a lot of room to take on stress. Also suited for those cleaning up bodyfat in a gaining phase. This should be used with extreme caution, and I advise against the upper end of this range unless you're working with a coach and are very high in bodyfat."}]]},{"type":"columns","layout":"four","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Cutting</strong><br></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Cutting"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>0.5-1%</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"0.5-1%"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>375 - 750g loss</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"375 - 750g loss"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Suitable for anyone looking for a steadier and more moderate approach with less room to take on stress.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Suitable for anyone looking for a steadier and more moderate approach with less room to take on stress."}]]},{"type":"columns","layout":"four","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Maintenance/recomposition</strong><br></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"Maintenance/recomposition"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>0.1-02% loss to 01.-0.2% gain</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"0.1-02% loss to 01.-0.2% gain"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>75-150g loss - 75-150g gain</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","text":"75-150g loss - 75-150g gain"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Suitable for those fairly close to their goal and wanting to make gradual changes with minimal cost.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Suitable for those fairly close to their goal and wanting to make gradual changes with minimal cost."}]]},{"type":"columns","layout":"four","cols":[[{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>Gaining</strong><br></p>","text":"Gaining"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>0.25-0.5% gain</p>","text":"0.25-0.5% gain"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>190 - 350g gain</p>","text":"190 - 350g gain"}],[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Suitable for those wanting to build muscle. In general, I do not recommend choosing the upper end of this range unless you're going all in with training, have a very well designed program (Forge... hello?) and/or you're newbie that's a fair distance from your goal.</p>","text":"Suitable for those wanting to build muscle. In general, I do not recommend choosing the upper end of this range unless you're going all in with training, have a very well designed program (Forge... hello?) and/or you're newbie that's a fair distance from your goal."}]]},{"type":"text","html":"<p><br></p>Where you sit within the range is up to you, but it'll depend on a few factors.<p><br></p>","text":"Where you sit within the range is up to you, but it'll depend on a few factors."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before deciding on your rate...","html":"<p><em>Before deciding on your rate...</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>A few things to consider...</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Get-to-give. </strong>This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses. <br></p><p><br></p><strong>Proximity to goal. </strong>Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more 🤣<p><br></p><p><strong>Experience.</strong> My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears.\n<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Timeline. </strong>If you're short on time and feel you <em>need </em>to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet.</p><p><br></p><p>You might note the absence of an aggressive gain option. That's because aggressive gaining just means getting fatter faster and making more mess to clean up. Gaining's also something that needs a far longer lifespan than cutting, and since any aggressive diet demands a shorter timeline, it just doesn't work. There's no upside, so I'm not even making it an option.</p><p><br></p>","text":"A few things to consider...\nGet-to-give. This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses. \n\nProximity to goal. Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more 🤣\nExperience. My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears.\n\n\nTimeline. If you're short on time and feel you need to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet.\nYou might note the absence of an aggressive gain option. That's because aggressive gaining just means getting fatter faster and making more mess to clean up. Gaining's also something that needs a far longer lifespan than cutting, and since any aggressive diet demands a shorter timeline, it just doesn't work. There's no upside, so I'm not even making it an option."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Locking in.","html":"<p><em>Locking in.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.</p><p><br></p><p>This is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against.</p><p><br></p><p>Once we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros.</p>","text":"Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.\nThis is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against.\nOnce we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros."}]}]},{"id":"the-case-for-rinse-and-repeat-eating","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985126632-2a566bda2640aa0563c6a1954a0bc3cbdd5e11fcb56407bee5be3fea8f16dfec-d_1280x720?region=us","n":27,"title":"The case for rinse and repeat eating.","m":4,"vimeo":"1058558889","dur":231,"code":"0505","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","The case for rinse and repeat eating."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Eating the same thing every day don't sound all that 'eatable'.<br></p>","text":"Eating the same thing every day don't sound all that 'eatable'."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>So why the hell am I saying you should do it? 🧐</strong><br></p>","text":"So why the hell am I saying you should do it? 🧐"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Because it might be <em>the slickest move you can make </em>when you start a new diet. </p><p><br></p><p>Let me break it down for you...<br></p>","text":"Because it might be the slickest move you can make when you start a new diet. \nLet me break it down for you..."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058558889","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058558889?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"i-dont-give-a-fig-what-you-weigh-and-neither-should-you","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985126823-1c74e7a7b4a967e304d6af40a775ad979e562aa476a7878da7fc3cb07a8fc3dd-d_1280x720?region=us","n":28,"title":"I don't give a fig what you weigh (and neither should you)...","m":4,"vimeo":"1058562571","dur":155,"code":"0506","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","I don't give a fig what you weigh (and neither should you)..."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Hang on a second...<br></p>","text":"Hang on a second..."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>If weight is how we know things are working, then it <em>has </em>to matter... right?</strong><strong>🤨</strong></p>","text":"If weight is how we know things are working, then it has to matter... right?🤨"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Good question. Let me explain...<br></p>","text":"Good question. Let me explain..."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058562571","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058562571?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><br></p><p><strong>Remember: </strong>your scale weight is going to change, but what you see between your toes each morning isn't always the best reflection of what you actually weigh.<br></p>","text":"Remember: your scale weight is going to change, but what you see between your toes each morning isn't always the best reflection of what you actually weigh."},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fscale-1739782521.png","file":"scale-1739782521.png","alt":"","route":"scale"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The golden rule is this:<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Don't worry about your weight</em>. Assess the average, and trust the trend.</strong><br></p>","text":"The golden rule is this:\n\nDon't worry about your weight. Assess the average, and trust the trend."}]},{"id":"this-sections-secrets-3","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985127097-35977363b0a0614d01368fe63a635721c92af4907673b5d6e1588686b0447c31-d_1280x720?region=us","n":29,"title":"This section's secrets.","m":4,"vimeo":"1058561775","dur":84,"code":"0507","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW)","This section's secrets."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"It's been a BIG section. Let's review.","text":"It's been a BIG section. Let's review."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058561775","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058561775?badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Here's this section's upgrades...","html":"<p><br>Here's this section's upgrades...</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<strong>1. There's ONE WAY to know if your plan's working... </strong>but progress <u>can’t be treated as binary</u>: it has to be at the right pace, or you might get yourself stuck in the progress trap.<p><br></p><p><strong>2. To stay out of the progress trap, </strong><strong><em>use this formula:</em></strong> Set a rate and plan &gt; Execute and track your progress &gt; Adjust when you miss &gt; Rinse and repeat.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>3. How fast you get jacked IS TOTALLY UP TO YOU. </strong>But it’s vital you know what it is before you start. Slow’s easy, but slow. Fast is hard, and comes with more cost. Pick your poison, but never miss the mark.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>4. Rinse and repeat what you eat at the start of every new diet.</strong> It makes reading whether you’re getting the right results a lot easier to do, but you don’t have to do it permanently.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>5. Your weight doesn’t really matter,</strong> unless your sport demands it. Otherwise, our rule is to assess the average, and track the trend.</p>","text":"1. There's ONE WAY to know if your plan's working... but progress can’t be treated as binary: it has to be at the right pace, or you might get yourself stuck in the progress trap.\n2. To stay out of the progress trap, use this formula: Set a rate and plan > Execute and track your progress > Adjust when you miss > Rinse and repeat.\n3. How fast you get jacked IS TOTALLY UP TO YOU. But it’s vital you know what it is before you start. Slow’s easy, but slow. Fast is hard, and comes with more cost. Pick your poison, but never miss the mark.\n4. Rinse and repeat what you eat at the start of every new diet. It makes reading whether you’re getting the right results a lot easier to do, but you don’t have to do it permanently.\n5. Your weight doesn’t really matter, unless your sport demands it. Otherwise, our rule is to assess the average, and track the trend."}]},{"id":"the-skinny-on-eating-like-a-fatty","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985130799-ea433c175a64ce24b1608b549b35eb21ff7ed47e8ee20b2554f67eca9c379d8e-d_1280x720?region=us","n":30,"title":"The skinny on eating like a fatty.","m":5,"vimeo":"1058564468","dur":22,"code":"0601","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT CAKE","The skinny on eating like a fatty."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>We can't bang on about a Repeatable approach and <em>not </em>have a strategy for real life. Because sometimes...<br></p>","text":"We can't bang on about a Repeatable approach and not have a strategy for real life. Because sometimes..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Girls boys DOGGIES JUST WANNA HAVE FUN 🤣","html":"<p><s>Girls</s> <s>boys</s> DOGGIES JUST WANNA HAVE FUN 🤣<br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>So when life gives you cake... I say you should eat it.</p><p>You just need to know <em>how. </em>Which is why I'm going to show you. In this section, we'll cover...</p>","text":"So when life gives you cake... I say you should eat it.You just need to know how. Which is why I'm going to show you. In this section, we'll cover..."},{"type":"text","html":"<ul><li><strong>How to bake a bit of fun into your life</strong> and <u>still get jacked.</u>..</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>How to get away with eating cake </strong>and who I recommend this strategy for...</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>And when putting ice cream first</strong> is the right idea 🍦</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Shall we?</p>","text":"How to bake a bit of fun into your life and still get jacked...\nHow to get away with eating cake and who I recommend this strategy for...\nAnd when putting ice cream first is the right idea 🍦\nShall we?"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058564468","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058564468?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"got-cake","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985130398-20ff34d0de86ee6f7a0ef0e65faba06aa121617d64f3f562d5d6d014f62639f5-d_1280x720?region=us","n":31,"title":"Got cake?","m":5,"vimeo":"1058564685","dur":67,"code":"0602","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT CAKE","Got cake?"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Or cheeseburgers. Or drinks with friends. Or a good, balanced life. </p><p><br></p><p>It's not all about cake...</p>","text":"Or cheeseburgers. Or drinks with friends. Or a good, balanced life. \nIt's not all about cake..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"It's about a real life's 'what if' scenarios...","html":"<p>It's about a real life's '<em>what if' </em>scenarios...<br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><em>What if I need me a sweet treat? </em></p><p><em>What if I just gotta mix it up sometimes? </em></p><p><em>What if Tuesday night is date night? </em></p><p><em>What if my grandmother'll murder me if I don't have three serves?</em><br></p><p><br></p><p>Here's how to deal with them 😇</p>","text":"What if I need me a sweet treat? What if I just gotta mix it up sometimes? What if Tuesday night is date night? What if my grandmother'll murder me if I don't have three serves?\n\nHere's how to deal with them 😇"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058564685","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058564685?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]},{"id":"eat-the-damn-thing","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985129412-f2d098a460085308f2243072d54b498eb71e4e70f8145eb3ea900ab4efbcbe07-d_1280x720?region=us","n":32,"title":"EAT the damn thing!","m":5,"vimeo":"1058565466","dur":220,"code":"0603","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT CAKE","EAT the damn thing!"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>And consider this permission 😎</p><p><br></p><p>As long as you do it how I show you, that is...</p>","text":"And consider this permission 😎\nAs long as you do it how I show you, that is..."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058565466","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058565466?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Eat the cake.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Eat the cake.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>If you've considered your tendencies and preferences, and you think this approach is a fit for you, great. Here's how to put it to work.</p><p><br></p>","text":"If you've considered your tendencies and preferences, and you think this approach is a fit for you, great. Here's how to put it to work."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Decide on a cadence.","html":"<p><em>Step One — Decide on a cadence.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Pick how frequently you'll allow yourself to break from plan. Given that we're making no adjustment to your other targets or to your diet in general, I recommend something north of once per fortnight.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Pick how frequently you'll allow yourself to break from plan. Given that we're making no adjustment to your other targets or to your diet in general, I recommend something north of once per fortnight."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Monitor.","html":"<p><em>Step Two — Monitor.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Make sure that the size and cadence of your 'cake' meals aren't rocking the boat. If you're consistently hitting your target change rate, you can keep trucking. But if you find that your progress is taking a hit, you'll need to either be more conservative with your meals or the frequency of them.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Make sure that the size and cadence of your 'cake' meals aren't rocking the boat. If you're consistently hitting your target change rate, you can keep trucking. But if you find that your progress is taking a hit, you'll need to either be more conservative with your meals or the frequency of them."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Adjust and repeat.","html":"<p><em>Step Three — Adjust and repeat.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Repeat these steps, always putting your rate of progress above making your diet fun. We've got a job to do, and that comes first.</p>","text":"Repeat these steps, always putting your rate of progress above making your diet fun. We've got a job to do, and that comes first."}]}]},{"id":"when-you-should-eat-your-ice-cream-first","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985128611-fbc4c8711cf80323679280c6823ccbcd73545ef8f55dd3d5168c759ad8573eb2-d_1280x720?region=us","n":33,"title":"When you should eat your ice cream first.","m":5,"vimeo":"1058567784","dur":133,"code":"0604","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT CAKE","When you should eat your ice cream first."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Call me crazy...</p>","text":"Call me crazy..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"But sometimes you should start with your soft serve... 🥳","html":"<p>But sometimes you should start with your soft serve... 🥳<br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"In this video, I'll break down who this approach is for, when to use it, and how it works.","text":"In this video, I'll break down who this approach is for, when to use it, and how it works."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058567784","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058567784?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"FLYWHEEL — Ice cream first.","html":"<p>FLYWHEEL — Ice cream first.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>If you're like me and want more flex with more frequency, this is your approach. We definitely do not need instructions for this, but I put a little grey box around every other action step and I'll be damned if one of my modules doesn't match 🙃<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"If you're like me and want more flex with more frequency, this is your approach. We definitely do not need instructions for this, but I put a little grey box around every other action step and I'll be damned if one of my modules doesn't match 🙃"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Add an 'ice cream' layer to your pyramid.","html":"<p><em>Step One — Add an 'ice cream' layer to your pyramid.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Remember, it doesn't have to be ice cream. Whatever value add makes things work for you is great, as long as it doesn't break any of the Three Laws.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Remember, it doesn't have to be ice cream. Whatever value add makes things work for you is great, as long as it doesn't break any of the Three Laws."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Go back to the usual priorities.","html":"<p><em>Step Two — Go back to the usual priorities.</em><br></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Plan out the rest of your budget in accordance with the usual steps. But like I said in the last step — if this interferes with your ability to build properly or breaks the laws, be more cautious about your 'ice cream' next time.</p>","text":"Plan out the rest of your budget in accordance with the usual steps. But like I said in the last step — if this interferes with your ability to build properly or breaks the laws, be more cautious about your 'ice cream' next time."}]}]},{"id":"ground-rules-for-good-livin","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985128364-7a91898806bc3ffecda2bc780eff9fde0480292e7d2b96685b10dcadf772e37e-d_1280x720?region=us","n":34,"title":"Ground rules for good livin'.","m":5,"vimeo":"1058570033","dur":178,"code":"0605","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO EAT CAKE","Ground rules for good livin'."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"If you're gonna bake in some fun, here are a few little rules to follow.<p><br></p><p>It's your world, but let's just make sure you don't get too buck wild or make problems for yourself 😝</p>","text":"If you're gonna bake in some fun, here are a few little rules to follow.\nIt's your world, but let's just make sure you don't get too buck wild or make problems for yourself 😝"},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058570033","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058570033?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Ground Rules","html":"<p><br>The Ground Rules</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>1. Do not break the laws.</strong><br></p>","text":"1. Do not break the laws."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Yes, we want eatable. But if you go too eatable, it might mess with repeatable. And if that happens, <em>kiss the results goodbye.</em></p><p><br></p>","text":"Yes, we want eatable. But if you go too eatable, it might mess with repeatable. And if that happens, kiss the results goodbye."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>2. DBAD.</strong><br></p>","text":"2. DBAD."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Don't. Be. A. Dummy*.</p><p><br></p><p><u>It's not party time when you diet</u>. Yes, you're allowed to have some 'nice'. But dieting is a short term thing. <em>We're here to get a job done</em>, so we can get back to real life with a new and improved rig. Don't forget what we're doing here.</p><p><br></p><p>Two ways to look at it. If you'd be a little timid eating that treat in front of the Top Doggie, you're being at twit. And if the other non-dieting, healthy adults at the table aren't eating that way, it's a good sign you shouldn't be, either.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Don't. Be. A. Dummy*.\nIt's not party time when you diet. Yes, you're allowed to have some 'nice'. But dieting is a short term thing. We're here to get a job done, so we can get back to real life with a new and improved rig. Don't forget what we're doing here.\nTwo ways to look at it. If you'd be a little timid eating that treat in front of the Top Doggie, you're being at twit. And if the other non-dieting, healthy adults at the table aren't eating that way, it's a good sign you shouldn't be, either."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>3. Don't blow your cals (sorta).</strong><br></p>","text":"3. Don't blow your cals (sorta)."},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Unless you're eating the cake. Then (as long as its at your set cadence) you're okay.</p>","text":"Unless you're eating the cake. Then (as long as its at your set cadence) you're okay."}]},{"id":"how-to-put-it-all-together","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985263071-33703242c13f802908d3507ca41086796c12c08cbfc526afa688a9146a98c6dd-d_1280x720?region=us","n":35,"title":"How to put it all together.","m":6,"vimeo":"1058570866","dur":22,"code":"0701","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO PUT INMRS TO WORK","How to put it all together."],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>This is the walkthrough! For a step-by-step instructional, see below.</p>","text":"This is the walkthrough! For a step-by-step instructional, see below."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058570866","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058570866?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Putting it all together.","html":"<p><br>Putting it all together.</p>"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>This is for the suckers that didn't play along like they got told to. Or, for the attention-to-detail types that wanna check they got it all right. Either way, I got you 😘</p><p><br></p><p>Here's all the stuff we hit, and all our flywheel steps.</p><p><br></p>","text":"This is for the suckers that didn't play along like they got told to. Or, for the attention-to-detail types that wanna check they got it all right. Either way, I got you 😘\nHere's all the stuff we hit, and all our flywheel steps."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong>HOW TO GET STARTED</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO GET STARTED"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The INMRS philosophy is simple: proactive planning DOGWALKS reactive tracking and makes nailing macros with YOUR OWN diet an absolute breeze.</p><p><br></p><p>The system is built off adhering to INMRS' Three Laws. They are:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Law One. </strong>Make it eatable. </p><p><br></p><p><strong> Law Two. </strong>Make it repeatable. </p><p> </p><p><strong>Law Three. </strong>Make it effective.</p><p><br></p><p>You follow those, and you'll always be on track.<br></p>","text":"The INMRS philosophy is simple: proactive planning DOGWALKS reactive tracking and makes nailing macros with YOUR OWN diet an absolute breeze.\nThe system is built off adhering to INMRS' Three Laws. They are:\nLaw One. Make it eatable. \n Law Two. Make it repeatable.  Law Three. Make it effective.\nYou follow those, and you'll always be on track."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"1. FLYWHEEL — Do this now.","html":"<p>1. FLYWHEEL — Do this now.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Buy your tools. Get yourself:<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>A set of digital kitchen scales</strong>. I have a big set and a little set.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A set of digital bathroom scales.</strong> They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A macro tracking app.</strong> I recommend MacroFactor highly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A tape measure.</strong> This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Buy your tools. Get yourself:\n\nA set of digital kitchen scales. I have a big set and a little set.\nA set of digital bathroom scales. They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea.\nA macro tracking app. I recommend MacroFactor highly.\nA tape measure. This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br>HOW TO CALCULATE YOUR MACROS</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO CALCULATE YOUR MACROS"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Macro calculators <em>suck </em>when it comes to getting you perfect targets. But they're perfectly reliable for targets that are in the right ballpark and serve as a starting point to fine tune. </p><p><br></p><p>To get a good starting point set of macros — or more specifically — starting point calorie and protein targets (since they're what really drives success), you <em>need </em>to know your bodyfat.</p><p><br></p><p>There are a few ways to calculate it, and all you need is a decent estimate. But once you've got it, you can trust your macros are solid.<br></p>","text":"Macro calculators suck when it comes to getting you perfect targets. But they're perfectly reliable for targets that are in the right ballpark and serve as a starting point to fine tune. \nTo get a good starting point set of macros — or more specifically — starting point calorie and protein targets (since they're what really drives success), you need to know your bodyfat.\nThere are a few ways to calculate it, and all you need is a decent estimate. But once you've got it, you can trust your macros are solid."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"2. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your bodyfat.","html":"<p>2. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your bodyfat.<s></s></p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>There are three ways to come up with a bodyfat estimate.</p><p><br></p>","text":"There are three ways to come up with a bodyfat estimate."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"DEXA Scan","html":"<p>DEXA Scan</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a fancy X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months.  </p><p><br></p><p>To get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with...</p><p><br></p>","text":"DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a fancy X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months.  \nTo get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Naval Method","html":"<p>The Naval Method</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and an online calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.  </p><p><br></p><p>All your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:  </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Neck</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure at the base of your neck. <br></p><p><strong>Waist</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure across the navel. </p><p><strong>Hips (female only)</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.  </p><p><br></p><p>I recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. Then, head to the <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/naval\">https://bthr.rodeo/naval</a> and enter your measurements to get an estimate of your bodyfat. </p><p> </p><p>While you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with...</p><p><br></p>","text":"The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and an online calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.  \nAll your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:  \nNeck - Measure at the base of your neck. \nWaist - Measure across the navel. Hips (female only) - Measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.  \nI recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. Then, head to the https://bthr.rodeo/naval and enter your measurements to get an estimate of your bodyfat.  While you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Visual Method","html":"<p>The Visual Method</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate. </p><p> </p><p><strong>1. Take a clear full-body photo of yourself.</strong> Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo. <br><br></p><p><strong>2. Compare it to a body fat percentage chart. </strong>Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts. <br><br></p><p><strong>3. Look at key areas. </strong>Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different. <br><br></p><p><strong>4. Find your match.</strong> Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution.<br></p>","text":"This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate.  1. Take a clear full-body photo of yourself. Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo. \n\n2. Compare it to a body fat percentage chart. Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts. \n\n3. Look at key areas. Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different. \n\n4. Find your match. Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution."}]},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"3. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your macros.","html":"<p>3. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your macros.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Now, crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros.  <p>Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it. </p> <p>Otherwise, go to <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/macros\">https://bthr.rodeo/macros</a> for an online calculator. Under the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat. </p> <p>Once you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move.</p>","text":"Now, crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros.  Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it.  Otherwise, go to https://bthr.rodeo/macros for an online calculator. Under the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat.  Once you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br>HOW TO TURN 'EM INTO A MENU</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO TURN 'EM INTO A MENU"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Once you've got macros, making a menu <em>always </em>starts with what you actually want to eat. </p><p><br></p><p>Smart players will learn to integrate what they want with what's great for them and their long term health, but to begin with, we start where you and your current lifestyle are at, and what's familiar and realistic for you. You'll kick off there - by putting together a wish list menu of foods you know you'll be happy (enough) to eat.</p><p><br></p><p>Once we've got your wish list menu, we use a budget-style system to make sure you've got your priorities straight and synced with what works. Dieting's hard, and the body pushes back. But executing our priorities in order and in accordance with the pro level mindset that suits our diet and its challenges, we put all the calorie 'cash' to the big, important stuff first, and 'spend' in a strategic fashion.</p>","text":"Once you've got macros, making a menu always starts with what you actually want to eat. \nSmart players will learn to integrate what they want with what's great for them and their long term health, but to begin with, we start where you and your current lifestyle are at, and what's familiar and realistic for you. You'll kick off there - by putting together a wish list menu of foods you know you'll be happy (enough) to eat.\nOnce we've got your wish list menu, we use a budget-style system to make sure you've got your priorities straight and synced with what works. Dieting's hard, and the body pushes back. But executing our priorities in order and in accordance with the pro level mindset that suits our diet and its challenges, we put all the calorie 'cash' to the big, important stuff first, and 'spend' in a strategic fashion."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"4. FLYWHEEL — The wish list menu.","html":"<p>4. FLYWHEEL — The wish list menu.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Here's how to put together your wish list menu.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Here's how to put together your wish list menu."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.","html":"<p>Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.  </p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page. </p> <p>Giving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page.  Giving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.","html":"<p>Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p> Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on. </p><p><br></p>","text":"Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Write out the menu.","html":"<p>Step Three — Write out the menu.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>And remember that the only criteria you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?  </p><p><br></p><p>Don't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.  </p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Start by naming what you're eating.</strong> Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch. <br><br></p><p><strong>2. Write out each ingredient.</strong> Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on. <br><br></p><p><strong>3. Include the details.</strong> Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.  </p><p><br></p><p>But again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there.\n</p>","text":"And remember that the only criteria you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?  \nDon't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.  \n1. Start by naming what you're eating. Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch. \n\n2. Write out each ingredient. Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on. \n\n3. Include the details. Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.  \nBut again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there."}]},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"5. FLYWHEEL — Building your menu.","html":"<p>5. FLYWHEEL — Building your menu.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.  <p>But before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities.</p><p><br></p>","text":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.  But before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Identify your first priority.","html":"<p>Step One — Identify your first priority.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now.\n<p><br></p>","text":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Track it.","html":"<p>Step Two — Track it.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.  <p>If you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that. </p> <p>At the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range. </p> <p>Don't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.  If you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that.  At the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range.  Don't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Rinse and repeat.","html":"<p>Step Three — Rinse and repeat.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.  <p>And that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu.</p>","text":"Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.  And that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br>HOW TO TRACK RIGHT</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO TRACK RIGHT"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>To keep it short and sweet, tracking right is tracking consistently and tracking accurately. That's it. No magic.</p><p><br></p><p>But the biggest, most common, most insidious and most damaging to make, BAR NONE, is lying to yourself. Don't convince yourself that tracking doesn't work because <em>you didn't work it right</em>. Right? Right.</p><p><br></p><p>There's a bunch of friction when you start tracking. Interfacing with a new app, finding foods, an extra step being added to eating, and so on. What we want is accuracy, consistency and simplicity in our tracking approach. </p><p><br></p><p>There are also a number of really typical traps most trackers fall into. It ain't the end of the world because you'll learn faster if you make mistakes. The name of the game's not never messing up — it's being <strong>lightning fast with identification, and even faster with course correction</strong>. The slicker you get at catching and correcting mistakes, the better you'll be at this.</p><p><br></p><p>If you're someone that's got a track record of going off track, the mindset shift that'll level you up is this: <strong>be a curious observer</strong>. Watch <em>why </em>you do things instead of getting mad when you do them and creating a blindspot for yourself.</p><p><br></p>","text":"To keep it short and sweet, tracking right is tracking consistently and tracking accurately. That's it. No magic.\nBut the biggest, most common, most insidious and most damaging to make, BAR NONE, is lying to yourself. Don't convince yourself that tracking doesn't work because you didn't work it right. Right? Right.\nThere's a bunch of friction when you start tracking. Interfacing with a new app, finding foods, an extra step being added to eating, and so on. What we want is accuracy, consistency and simplicity in our tracking approach. \nThere are also a number of really typical traps most trackers fall into. It ain't the end of the world because you'll learn faster if you make mistakes. The name of the game's not never messing up — it's being lightning fast with identification, and even faster with course correction. The slicker you get at catching and correcting mistakes, the better you'll be at this.\nIf you're someone that's got a track record of going off track, the mindset shift that'll level you up is this: be a curious observer. Watch why you do things instead of getting mad when you do them and creating a blindspot for yourself."},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>HOW TO CHECK THEY'RE WORKING</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO CHECK THEY'RE WORKING"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The ONLY metric that matters is... are you getting jacked? But that's not some cutesy take — there's more. Progress can not be treated as binary, and we need to be getting jacked at the right pace to make sure we don't fall into the progress trap.<br></p><p><br></p><p>To do so, we need to know our personal rate of progress, as determined by considering a few factors and finding what works for you and your circumstances. </p><p><br></p><p>But we're relying heavily on what you weigh to make sure your menu and macros are working, which means having reliable weigh ins are an important factor. </p><p><br></p><p>Your weight's made up of both short-term and long-term weight — weight that's moving through you (like food and water) versus actually you (muscle, bone, organ, fat). The short-term weight fluctuates a lot depending on a number of factors and makes getting a read on your rate of progress more difficult. The most controllable of these factors is what you eat.</p><p><br></p><p>If you want reliable weigh ins, eating the same thing every day is a good idea. It only needs to be for the first few weeks while you get a read on your body's response. The more experienced and familiar you are with how your body responds to certain macros, the more confident you can be in the effect of your diet without needing this step.</p><p><br></p><p>Just remember, what you weigh doesn't matter. We care that it <em>changes. </em>The rule of thumb is <strong>don't worry about what you weigh. Assess the average, and trust the trend.</strong></p><p><strong><br></strong></p>","text":"The ONLY metric that matters is... are you getting jacked? But that's not some cutesy take — there's more. Progress can not be treated as binary, and we need to be getting jacked at the right pace to make sure we don't fall into the progress trap.\n\nTo do so, we need to know our personal rate of progress, as determined by considering a few factors and finding what works for you and your circumstances. \nBut we're relying heavily on what you weigh to make sure your menu and macros are working, which means having reliable weigh ins are an important factor. \nYour weight's made up of both short-term and long-term weight — weight that's moving through you (like food and water) versus actually you (muscle, bone, organ, fat). The short-term weight fluctuates a lot depending on a number of factors and makes getting a read on your rate of progress more difficult. The most controllable of these factors is what you eat.\nIf you want reliable weigh ins, eating the same thing every day is a good idea. It only needs to be for the first few weeks while you get a read on your body's response. The more experienced and familiar you are with how your body responds to certain macros, the more confident you can be in the effect of your diet without needing this step.\nJust remember, what you weigh doesn't matter. We care that it changes. The rule of thumb is don't worry about what you weigh. Assess the average, and trust the trend."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"6. FLYWHEEL — Set your rate of progress.","html":"<p>6. FLYWHEEL — Set your rate of progress.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.\n</p><p><br></p>","text":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Know the rates.","html":"<p>Step One — Know the rates.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.<p><br></p><p>They range from weekly losses of 2.5% of your bodyweight, through to weekly gain of 0.5% of your bodyweight, depending on your goal and the factors outlined below.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.\nThey range from weekly losses of 2.5% of your bodyweight, through to weekly gain of 0.5% of your bodyweight, depending on your goal and the factors outlined below."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Before deciding on your rate...","html":"<p>Step Two — Before deciding on your rate...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"A few things to consider...  <p><strong>Get-to-give.</strong> This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses. </p> <p><strong>Proximity to goal.</strong> Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more </p> <p><strong>Experience.</strong> My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears. </p> <p><strong>Timeline. </strong>If you're short on time and feel you need to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet. </p><p><br></p>","text":"A few things to consider...  Get-to-give. This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses.  Proximity to goal. Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more  Experience. My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears.  Timeline. If you're short on time and feel you need to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Locking in.","html":"<p>Step Three — Locking in.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.  <p>This is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against. </p> <p>Once we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros.\n</p>","text":"Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.  This is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against.  Once we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p><strong><br>HOW TO EAT CAKE</strong><br></p>","text":"HOW TO EAT CAKE"},{"type":"divider"},{"type":"text","html":"It's not all about cake.  It's about the 'what if' situations... <p><br></p><p><em>What if</em> I need me a sweet treat? </p><p><em>What if</em> I just gotta mix it up sometimes? </p><p><em>What if</em> Tuesday night is date night? </p><p><em>What if</em> my grandmother'll murder me if I don't have three serves?</p><p><br></p><p>It ain't wise to go into things with an all-or-nothing, perfect-or-bust approach. There are two strategies I recommend for baking a bit of fun into your life, and making sure there's room to be a real person.</p><p><br></p>","text":"It's not all about cake.  It's about the 'what if' situations... \nWhat if I need me a sweet treat? What if I just gotta mix it up sometimes? What if Tuesday night is date night? What if my grandmother'll murder me if I don't have three serves?\nIt ain't wise to go into things with an all-or-nothing, perfect-or-bust approach. There are two strategies I recommend for baking a bit of fun into your life, and making sure there's room to be a real person."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Strategy One — If you've got cake? Eat it.","html":"<p>Strategy One — If you've got cake? Eat it.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Have fun. Order the burger. Drink the beer. Eat the cake.<p><br></p><p>Don't skip meals, save macros, or 'train it off' later. For one meal to have any kind of impact, you'd have to be so unbelievably reckless and outta line for someone with a goal. And even then, as an isolated event, the impact will be tiny. If you're not being a twit, then just 'eating the cake' won't make a dent. Your short-term weight'll spike and then it'll be back down within a few days.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>To use this approach...</strong></p><p> Substitute your 'cake' meal in for your usual one, or don't. It's helpful to choose something that has equivalent protein if that's an option, or to crank up protein elsewhere. If you can't for a day, no big deal. Decide on a cadence that works for you — once every few weeks, or whatever you find doesn't rock the boat for your rate of progress.</p> <p><strong>Who it suits...</strong></p><p>If you prefer to nail your plan and be on track 95% of the time, this is for you. You like order and structure, and knowing you've got a plan for when real life happens.</p><p><br><strong>What to watch out for...</strong><strong><br></strong></p><p> If you're an all-or-nothing thinker that tends to get carried away the moment they're not on plan, this strategy isn't right for you.<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Have fun. Order the burger. Drink the beer. Eat the cake.\nDon't skip meals, save macros, or 'train it off' later. For one meal to have any kind of impact, you'd have to be so unbelievably reckless and outta line for someone with a goal. And even then, as an isolated event, the impact will be tiny. If you're not being a twit, then just 'eating the cake' won't make a dent. Your short-term weight'll spike and then it'll be back down within a few days.\nTo use this approach... Substitute your 'cake' meal in for your usual one, or don't. It's helpful to choose something that has equivalent protein if that's an option, or to crank up protein elsewhere. If you can't for a day, no big deal. Decide on a cadence that works for you — once every few weeks, or whatever you find doesn't rock the boat for your rate of progress. Who it suits...If you prefer to nail your plan and be on track 95% of the time, this is for you. You like order and structure, and knowing you've got a plan for when real life happens.\nWhat to watch out for...\n If you're an all-or-nothing thinker that tends to get carried away the moment they're not on plan, this strategy isn't right for you."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Strategy Two — The 'ice cream first' approach","html":"<p>Strategy Two — The 'ice cream first' approach</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"For a little more flex a little more frequently, put your ice cream first.<p><br></p><p>What your 'ice cream' might be is totally up to you:</p><ul><li>Dinner with the family</li><li>A date night with your spouse</li><li>A Chokito bar and a cuppa before bed</li><li>Or whatever else makes your diet appropriately eatable</li></ul> But if you're shaking things up on a more regular basis, we'll need to build it into the plan to stay on pace.<br><p><br></p><p><strong>To use this approach...</strong><br></p><p> Add a layer to the bottom of your priority pyramid, and plan your ice cream first. It might be something you do a few times a month, or even every day (as long as it doesn't mess with repeatability and results). Once you've done so, get back to building the rest of your menu with your other priorities.<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Who it suits...</strong></p><p>This is for social eaters, all-or-nothing thinkers and foodies. If waiting weeks between fun meals would make you lose your mind and fall off your plan, you should put your ice cream first.<strong><br></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>What to watch out for...</strong></p><p> This approach will mean big impact on your short-term weight, and having a harder time reading what's actually happening with your long-term weight. Its also easy to get carried away and find yourself making irresponsible decisions just because you can make things fit your macros. Be careful and considered, and don't get carried away.<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"For a little more flex a little more frequently, put your ice cream first.\nWhat your 'ice cream' might be is totally up to you:Dinner with the familyA date night with your spouseA Chokito bar and a cuppa before bedOr whatever else makes your diet appropriately eatable But if you're shaking things up on a more regular basis, we'll need to build it into the plan to stay on pace.\n\nTo use this approach...\n Add a layer to the bottom of your priority pyramid, and plan your ice cream first. It might be something you do a few times a month, or even every day (as long as it doesn't mess with repeatability and results). Once you've done so, get back to building the rest of your menu with your other priorities.\n\nWho it suits...This is for social eaters, all-or-nothing thinkers and foodies. If waiting weeks between fun meals would make you lose your mind and fall off your plan, you should put your ice cream first.\n\nWhat to watch out for... This approach will mean big impact on your short-term weight, and having a harder time reading what's actually happening with your long-term weight. Its also easy to get carried away and find yourself making irresponsible decisions just because you can make things fit your macros. Be careful and considered, and don't get carried away."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The ground rules for good livin'.","html":"<p>The ground rules for good livin'.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>To keep you keeping on truckin', there are a few rules you gotta follow.<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Do not break the laws. </strong><strong> </strong></p><p>Yes, we want eatable. But if you go too eatable, it might mess with repeatable. And if that happens, kiss the results goodbye. </p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>2. DBAD. </strong><strong> </strong></p><p>Don't. Be. A. Dummy.\nIt's not party time when you diet. Yes, you're allowed to have some 'nice'. But dieting is a short term thing. We're here to get a job done, so we can get back to real life with a new and improved rig. Don't forget what we're doing here. </p> <p>Two ways to look at it. If you'd be a little timid eating that treat in front of the Top Doggie, you're being at twit. And if the other non-dieting, healthy adults at the table aren't eating that way, it's a good sign you shouldn't be, either. </p><p><strong> </strong></p><p><strong>3. Don't blow your cals (sorta). </strong><strong> </strong></p><p>Unless you're eating the cake. Then (as long as its at your set cadence) you're okay.<br></p>","text":"To keep you keeping on truckin', there are a few rules you gotta follow.\n\n1. Do not break the laws.  Yes, we want eatable. But if you go too eatable, it might mess with repeatable. And if that happens, kiss the results goodbye.  2. DBAD.  Don't. Be. A. Dummy.\nIt's not party time when you diet. Yes, you're allowed to have some 'nice'. But dieting is a short term thing. We're here to get a job done, so we can get back to real life with a new and improved rig. Don't forget what we're doing here.  Two ways to look at it. If you'd be a little timid eating that treat in front of the Top Doggie, you're being at twit. And if the other non-dieting, healthy adults at the table aren't eating that way, it's a good sign you shouldn't be, either.  3. Don't blow your cals (sorta).  Unless you're eating the cake. Then (as long as its at your set cadence) you're okay."},{"type":"group","kind":"box","blocks":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"7. FLYWHEEL — Eat cake, and avoid the progress trap.","html":"<p>7. FLYWHEEL — Eat cake, and avoid the progress trap.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>This one's a 1-2 combo.</p><p><br></p><p>You need to have a cake eating strategy (even if you don't plan on using it often), and we have to make sure your success isn't being messed with.</p><p><br></p>","text":"This one's a 1-2 combo.\nYou need to have a cake eating strategy (even if you don't plan on using it often), and we have to make sure your success isn't being messed with."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Pick a strategy.","html":"<p>Step One — Pick a strategy.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Pick whichever works for your preferences, and that you're most likely to comply with.<p><br></p>","text":"Pick whichever works for your preferences, and that you're most likely to comply with."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Stay out of the progress trap.","html":"<p>Step Two — Stay out of the progress trap.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Introducing change to your diet will almost always cause your weight to spike, and it'll be largely short term weight. But until you've got a good idea of how well your flexibility and formal plan are playing together, be careful not to write off all changes as just being short-term weight spikes. <br></p><p><br></p><p>If your average weight shows that you've missed your target, you'll either need to adjust your formal plan or your 'cake' plan (or both) to get back on track.<br></p>","text":"Introducing change to your diet will almost always cause your weight to spike, and it'll be largely short term weight. But until you've got a good idea of how well your flexibility and formal plan are playing together, be careful not to write off all changes as just being short-term weight spikes. \n\nIf your average weight shows that you've missed your target, you'll either need to adjust your formal plan or your 'cake' plan (or both) to get back on track."},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fdiagram-2-1740040852.png","file":"diagram-2-1740040852.png","alt":"","route":"loop"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Hop back to it.","html":"<p>Step Three — Hop back to it.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Once you've pivoted, go back to business as usual and keep monitoring. If progress is on pace, you're back on the gain train and with a new feather in your cap. If not, refine further and monitor again until you're back to moving at the right speed.","text":"Once you've pivoted, go back to business as usual and keep monitoring. If progress is on pace, you're back on the gain train and with a new feather in your cap. If not, refine further and monitor again until you're back to moving at the right speed."}]},{"type":"text","html":"<p>And that, doggie, is how to put it all together 😇</p>","text":"And that, doggie, is how to put it all together 😇"}]},{"id":"whats-next","thumb":"https://i.vimeocdn.com/video/1985128930-e1fd4b1c4d583326ab210d79cbce8d81981de3c66790cc825e530ff3c452fcb3-d_1280x720?region=us","n":36,"title":"What's next?","m":6,"vimeo":"1058571008","dur":114,"code":"0702","draft":false,"lifted":["HOW TO PUT INMRS TO WORK","What's next?"],"blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>That's up to you. If you execute, then the best shape you've <strong>ever been in <em></em></strong>awaits.</p><p><br></p><p>But before you go, just something I gotta say...</p>","text":"That's up to you. If you execute, then the best shape you've ever been in awaits.\nBut before you go, just something I gotta say..."},{"type":"video","vimeo":"1058571008","src":"https://player.vimeo.com/video/1058571008?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0&badge=0&autopause=0&player_id=0&app_id=58479"}]}],"v2":{"parts":[{"m":0,"ids":["how-i-lost-over-a-third-of-my-bodyweight-and-kept-it-off","the-most-valuable-video-of-inmrs-1","this-entire-course-on-a-page","how-to-get-an-absolutely-unreasonable-roi"]},{"m":1,"ids":["ground-zero","why-you-cant-trust-macro-calculators","wanna-instantly-screw-your-macros-do-this","just-how-fast-can-you-get-jacked","playing-on-expert-mode","this-sections-secrets"]},{"m":2,"ids":["this-is-the-end-of-crash-diets","the-big-rocks-budget","how-to-eat-whatever-the-hell-you-want-and-get-jacked-doing-it","this-might-piss-you-off","your-wish-list-menu-depends-on-this","the-exact-step-by-step-process","this-sections-secrets-1"]},{"m":3,"ids":["skip-this-to-screw-up-all-your-work","exactly-how-not-to-track","how-i-do-things-after-10-years","everyone-is-doing-this-stuff-wrong","this-sections-secrets-2"]},{"m":4,"ids":["were-not-here-to-lick-stamps","the-only-measure-that-really-matters","stay-out-of-the-progress-trap-for-good","the-case-for-rinse-and-repeat-eating","i-dont-give-a-fig-what-you-weigh-and-neither-should-you","this-sections-secrets-3"]},{"m":5,"ids":["the-skinny-on-eating-like-a-fatty","got-cake","eat-the-damn-thing","when-you-should-eat-your-ice-cream-first","keep-falling-off-the-wagon-watch-this","ground-rules-for-good-livin"]},{"m":6,"ids":["how-to-put-it-all-together","whats-next"]}],"hideDesk":true,"flywheel":true,"fly":[{"title":"1. FLYWHEEL — Do this now.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Buy your tools. Get yourself:<br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>A set of digital kitchen scales</strong>. I have a big set and a little set.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A set of digital bathroom scales.</strong> They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A macro tracking app.</strong> I recommend MacroFactor highly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>A tape measure.</strong> This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Buy your tools. Get yourself:\n\nA set of digital kitchen scales. I have a big set and a little set.\nA set of digital bathroom scales. They don't need to be flashy, and something cheap, effective and easily replaced is a good idea.\nA macro tracking app. I recommend MacroFactor highly.\nA tape measure. This one's a bonus and not necessary, but a handy tool to have for more complete progress tracking down the line."}]},{"title":"2. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your bodyfat.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>There are three ways to come up with a bodyfat estimate.</p><p><br></p>","text":"There are three ways to come up with a bodyfat estimate."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"DEXA Scan","html":"<p>DEXA Scan</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a fancy X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months.  </p><p><br></p><p>To get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with...</p><p><br></p>","text":"DEXA stands for Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry. It's a fancy X-ray that measures your bodyfat, muscle and bone density. It's accurate, and if you're a numbers nerd that likes really accurate progress tracking, I recommend getting one anywhere between every 3-12 months.  \nTo get one, just search 'DEXA scan near me'. But in my opinion, it's overkill for what we need. I'd go with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Naval Method","html":"<p>The Naval Method</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and an online calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.  </p><p><br></p><p>All your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:  </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Neck</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure at the base of your neck. <br></p><p><strong>Waist</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure across the navel. </p><p><strong>Hips (female only)</strong> <strong>-</strong> Measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.  </p><p><br></p><p>I recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. Then, head to the <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/naval\">https://bthr.rodeo/naval</a> and enter your measurements to get an estimate of your bodyfat. </p><p> </p><p>While you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with...</p><p><br></p>","text":"The Naval Method uses a few body measurements to get an estimate on your bodyfat. All you need is a tape measure and an online calculator to use it, and used correctly it's reasonably accurate.  \nAll your measurements must be taken with the tape completely level with the floor, and snug without being tight. You'll need your height, too, but the sites you're measuring are:  \nNeck - Measure at the base of your neck. \nWaist - Measure across the navel. Hips (female only) - Measure across the widest point of your hips and glutes.  \nI recommend having someone else take the measurements, and taking each one three times to get an average. Then, head to the https://bthr.rodeo/naval and enter your measurements to get an estimate of your bodyfat.  While you don't have to do both, you can be more confident in the estimate produced if you combine this with..."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Visual Method","html":"<p>The Visual Method</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate. </p><p> </p><p><strong>1. Take a clear full-body photo of yourself.</strong> Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo. <br><br></p><p><strong>2. Compare it to a body fat percentage chart. </strong>Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts. <br><br></p><p><strong>3. Look at key areas. </strong>Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different. <br><br></p><p><strong>4. Find your match.</strong> Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution.<br></p>","text":"This method is the quickest and easiest. It's as simple as making a comparison between your current shape and a series of reference images of people with accurately measured bodyfat. Because all people tend to carry bodyfat in different areas, I recommend comparing to a few for a more accurate estimate.  1. Take a clear full-body photo of yourself. Get in some decent light, use a tripod or someone you don't mind being in your undies in front of, and take a level, top-to-toe photo. \n\n2. Compare it to a body fat percentage chart. Or a few of them. Search 'visual bodyfat comparison' to find a few charts. \n\n3. Look at key areas. Compare abs, arms, chest, and lower body, because you might be built different. \n\n4. Find your match. Match your body shape to the closest percentage range on the chart. Ideally, you'll make your comparison to the body that you feel best matches your personal shape and distribution."}]},{"title":"3. FLYWHEEL — Calculating your macros.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"Now, crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros.  <p>Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it. </p> <p>Otherwise, go to <a href=\"https://bthr.rodeo/macros\">https://bthr.rodeo/macros</a> for an online calculator. Under the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat. </p> <p>Once you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move.</p>","text":"Now, crunch the numbers, baby. Let's get those macros.  Your tracking app almost definitely has a calculator built in, and as long as it allows you to calculate with bodyfat, you can use it.  Otherwise, go to https://bthr.rodeo/macros for an online calculator. Under the boxes to enter your stats, you'll see '+ Settings' in blue. Switch the BMR calculation to 'Katch-McArdle' and enter your bodyfat.  Once you're done, enter those first pass macros into your tracking app to set your targets and we're ready to move."}]},{"title":"4. FLYWHEEL — The wish list menu.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Here's how to put together your wish list menu.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Here's how to put together your wish list menu."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.","html":"<p>Step One — 'What I Want To Eat'.  </p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page. </p> <p>Giving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓<br></p><p><br></p>","text":"Set up the page and the right frame of mind. You're putting a big, meaty 'What I Want To Eat' at the top of the page.  Giving this a full step feels daft, but here we are 🤓"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.","html":"<p>Step Two — Set up your meal schedule.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p> Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on. </p><p><br></p>","text":"Now we want subheadings. Under your big one, write out the names of your meals (be that breakfast, lunch and dinner or Meal One, Two, Three). Next to them, note the times you typically like to eat and that suit your schedule, appetite, preferences and so on."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Write out the menu.","html":"<p>Step Three — Write out the menu.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>And remember that the only criteria you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?  </p><p><br></p><p>Don't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.  </p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Start by naming what you're eating.</strong> Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch. <br><br></p><p><strong>2. Write out each ingredient.</strong> Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on. <br><br></p><p><strong>3. Include the details.</strong> Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.  </p><p><br></p><p>But again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there.\n</p>","text":"And remember that the only criteria you're working with is... WOULD I LIKE TO EAT THAT?  \nDon't worry about anything else for now. If you want, feel free to test the system and get a little wild with it. Or, if you're stuck for what to do then just go with your usual foods.  \n1. Start by naming what you're eating. Under each meal header, write down the actual meal, such as 'chicken sando' for lunch. \n\n2. Write out each ingredient. Give each ingredient a line, and make sure you consider all of them. Main items, sauces, seasonings and condiments, oils for cooking and so on. \n\n3. Include the details. Be specific with the brand names and details, and if you've got an idea, the rough portion size or weight of each ingredient you use. If you're not sure on that right now, no stress. We'll tackle that soon.  \nBut again: don't get carried away here. This should take ten minutes, tops. Any longer and you're going too deep. Knock this first one out, and we'll go from there."}]},{"title":"5. FLYWHEEL — Building your menu.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.  <p>But before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities.</p><p><br></p>","text":"First up, get your tracking app open, and your wish list menu in front of you. Your macros should already be loaded up in your app, so we're ready to get stuck in.  But before we do, let me remind you. The pro mindset for your goal should be front of mind right now. As you work through this process, take a little time to consider how each choice you make gels with the pro mindset and what you know about your goal. Don't do anything that moves your menu out of line with Law One, but consider this as you work through your priorities."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Identify your first priority.","html":"<p>Step One — Identify your first priority.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now.\n<p><br></p>","text":"Comb through all the ingredients on your wish list menu, and identify the ones that are primarily protein sources. Some foods will have a good whack of trace protein, but we're really shooting for more 'pure' protein sources for now."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Track it.","html":"<p>Step Two — Track it.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.  <p>If you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that. </p> <p>At the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range. </p> <p>Don't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Enter all of your protein sources into your tracking app. Ignore everything else for now, and just load all your foods into the corresponding meals in your app, crossing them off on your wish list for clarity.  If you wrote your wish list menu with quantities of each ingredient, start with that. If you weren't sure, start with what's reasonable or you can search a typical portion size of that food, and go with that.  At the end of this process, we're looking to be within 10-20% of the day's target. If you've got a 150g protein target, we need to to be at 120-135g minimum before moving on to the next step. Depending on where you've landed after first entering all your protein foods, you'll need to scale the portions up or down to get within this range.  Don't fuss too hard over trying to perfectly land the target. Like we covered in the last step, other foods will have trace proteins, we've still got a fun layer to hopefully address, and with those two considerations we should end up covering anything that's missing."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Rinse and repeat.","html":"<p>Step Three — Rinse and repeat.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.  <p>And that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu.</p>","text":"Now, repeat using the next priority. Hit the following layer of your goal's pyramid, get within 10-20% by turning the portion dial up and down, and once you're in range, hit the next priority.  And that's that! At the end of this process, you should have a first pass menu."}]},{"title":"6. FLYWHEEL — Set your rate of progress.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.\n</p><p><br></p>","text":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Know the rates.","html":"<p>Step One — Know the rates.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.<p><br></p><p>They range from weekly losses of 2.5% of your bodyweight, through to weekly gain of 0.5% of your bodyweight, depending on your goal and the factors outlined below.</p><p><br></p>","text":"Remember, there's no one fixed rate for any goal. They're different depending on a couple of factors, but the primary one to consider is the give-to-get ratio. All of these numbers exist on a continuum from slow and easy through to hard and fast.\nThey range from weekly losses of 2.5% of your bodyweight, through to weekly gain of 0.5% of your bodyweight, depending on your goal and the factors outlined below."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Before deciding on your rate...","html":"<p>Step Two — Before deciding on your rate...</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"A few things to consider...  <p><strong>Get-to-give.</strong> This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses. </p> <p><strong>Proximity to goal.</strong> Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more </p> <p><strong>Experience.</strong> My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears. </p> <p><strong>Timeline. </strong>If you're short on time and feel you need to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet. </p><p><br></p>","text":"A few things to consider...  Get-to-give. This'll come up repeatedly, but remember that big returns come with big price tags. Cutting diets create stress. Gaining diets necessitate hard training that create stress. If you're already stressed, don't add big stresses.  Proximity to goal. Generally speaking, the further you are from your goal the more appropriate it is to choose a more aggressive rate. Your chances of responding positively and not copping too much pushback from your body are better, but you should still exercise caution. Going hard is always gonna hurt, or cost a bit more  Experience. My recommendation is ALWAYS to start more conservatively if you don't have experience. Aim low, and don't miss. Once you're reliably getting results, you've experienced the trade-offs, and you're happy with what you're seeing then you can shift gears.  Timeline. If you're short on time and feel you need to get to the goal faster, an aggressive rate will assist. Again, it'll come at more cost, and the other side of the coin is this: the harder you go, the shorter a lifespan of the diet."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Locking in.","html":"<p>Step Three — Locking in.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.  <p>This is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against. </p> <p>Once we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros.\n</p>","text":"Once you've weighed options, considered timelines and what's most suitable for you, lock in on your rate.  This is a mental exercise. At this point, we're not making any changes to your macro targets or menu. What we're doing is creating your personalised passing grade to measure your progress against.  Once we know what you need to see to call each week a win and stay out of the progress trap, we can spot when we're falling short, and stay safe from the progress trap by adjusting our macros."}]},{"title":"7. FLYWHEEL — Eat cake, and avoid the progress trap.","blocks":[{"type":"text","html":"<p>This one's a 1-2 combo.</p><p><br></p><p>You need to have a cake eating strategy (even if you don't plan on using it often), and we have to make sure your success isn't being messed with.</p><p><br></p>","text":"This one's a 1-2 combo.\nYou need to have a cake eating strategy (even if you don't plan on using it often), and we have to make sure your success isn't being messed with."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step One — Pick a strategy.","html":"<p>Step One — Pick a strategy.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Pick whichever works for your preferences, and that you're most likely to comply with.<p><br></p>","text":"Pick whichever works for your preferences, and that you're most likely to comply with."},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Two — Stay out of the progress trap.","html":"<p>Step Two — Stay out of the progress trap.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"<p>Introducing change to your diet will almost always cause your weight to spike, and it'll be largely short term weight. But until you've got a good idea of how well your flexibility and formal plan are playing together, be careful not to write off all changes as just being short-term weight spikes. <br></p><p><br></p><p>If your average weight shows that you've missed your target, you'll either need to adjust your formal plan or your 'cake' plan (or both) to get back on track.<br></p>","text":"Introducing change to your diet will almost always cause your weight to spike, and it'll be largely short term weight. But until you've got a good idea of how well your flexibility and formal plan are playing together, be careful not to write off all changes as just being short-term weight spikes. \n\nIf your average weight shows that you've missed your target, you'll either need to adjust your formal plan or your 'cake' plan (or both) to get back on track."},{"type":"image","src":"https://spark.thrivecart.com/0x0/user_assets%2FYLWU1D4J%2Fuploads%2Fimages%2Fdiagram-2-1740040852.png","file":"diagram-2-1740040852.png","alt":"","route":"loop"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step Three — Hop back to it.","html":"<p>Step Three — Hop back to it.</p>"},{"type":"text","html":"Once you've pivoted, go back to business as usual and keep monitoring. If progress is on pace, you're back on the gain train and with a new feather in your cap. If not, refine further and monitor again until you're back to moving at the right speed.","text":"Once you've pivoted, go back to business as usual and keep monitoring. If progress is on pace, you're back on the gain train and with a new feather in your cap. If not, refine further and monitor again until you're back to moving at the right speed."}]}],"flyPart":[0,1,1,2,2,4,5]},"moves":[{"what":"\"Just how fast can you get jacked?\" moves up, from HOW TO GET JACKED FAST (OR SLOW) into HOW TO SKIP THE ROOKIE MISTAKES, just before the calculator.","why":"The toolkit calculator asks for a goal (Aggressive Cut, Cut, Maintain, Gain) before it gives calories. In ThriveCart the lesson that explains those speeds comes 17 lessons later. Checked: the video (0504) never refers back to 0501–0503."},{"what":"\"Playing on expert mode.\" comes back in, after the speed lesson.","why":"It is a DRAFT in ThriveCart, so buyers never see it, and it is the only lesson with the toolkit download. Your call: it may be a draft on purpose."},{"what":"\"Keep falling off the wagon? Watch this.\" moves from HOW TO MAKE SURE IT WORKS to HOW TO EAT CAKE, before \"Ground rules for good livin'.\"","why":"The other tracking lessons are about weighing and logging. This one is about staying on, which is what the cake lessons and the ground rules are about. Checked: the video (0405) never refers to its neighbours."},{"what":"The three \"switch to desktop\" notes are hidden.","why":"They are true on ThriveCart and not true here: every lesson is built for a phone. A cut, not a rewrite."},{"what":"A \"Your flywheel\" page: the seven FLYWHEEL steps from \"How to put it all together.\" on one page, each with its own tick, reachable from every lesson.","why":"Course Genius, structure as value: the steps are the doing part of the course. In ThriveCart they sit inside one long lesson near the end. Words unchanged."}],"notes":{"the-most-valuable-video-of-inmrs-1":["The \"THIS COURSE SHOULD BE TAKEN ON A DESKTOP\" box is about ThriveCart. It is not true here. Kept word for word in v1; hidden in v2. Your call."],"playing-on-expert-mode":["DRAFT in ThriveCart: buyers do not see this lesson. It is the only one with the toolkit download. v1 hides it (as buyers see it); v2 brings it back. Your call."],"this-sections-secrets":["Four lessons share the title \"This section's secrets.\" (one has \"...\"). In a search list they look the same. A title idea is yours to write; flagged only."],"your-wish-list-menu-depends-on-this":["The two hand-drawn pyramids are now a pyramid you can tap, with a Cut ↔ Gain switch. Your drawings sit behind \"Original\". Route: interactive diagram.","Tier order is Claude's reading: bottom to top in the order of your rows beside each drawing (Protein first, Fun at the top), with calories and the pro mindset as the base. Your drawing has no labels on the tiers, so check it.","The \"switch to desktop\" note: not true here. Kept in v1, hidden in v2."],"just-how-fast-can-you-get-jacked":["The speed tool under this lesson is a copy of the BONUS 3 CALC build as it stood on 12 Nov. Its caps and logic are still open in that session; this copy updates when that one is copied again.","The \"switch to desktop\" note: not true here. Kept in v1, hidden in v2."],"stay-out-of-the-progress-trap-for-good":["The hand-drawn loop is redrawn in type, with a dot that walks the four steps. Your drawing sits behind \"Original\". Route: redraw."],"i-dont-give-a-fig-what-you-weigh-and-neither-should-you":["\"How scale weight works\" is now a week you can play with: switch \"In you\" off and the trend shows. Your drawing sits behind \"Original\". Route: interactive explainer.","The weights in it (80.0 kg falling to 79.4, with 0.5–2.0 kg \"in you\") are Claude's example, made up to match the shape of your bars. Yours to change."],"how-to-put-it-all-together":["Link fixed: the tape measure link was typed \"bthr/.rodeo/tape\" in ThriveCart and does not open there. Here it goes to bthr.rodeo/tape.","The loop drawing is the same one as in \"Stay OUT of the progress trap for good.\" Same redraw."],"how-i-do-things-after-10-years":[]},"toolkitSheet":"https://bthr.rodeo/inmrs/toolkit"};
